      "headline": "Development of Siculo-Arabic",
      "text": "Between 831 and 1091, Siculo-Arabic developed as a Maghrebi Arabic dialect in the Emirate of Sicily. This dialect is the precursor to the Maltese language.",
      "date": "0831"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Norman Invasion of Malta",
      "text": "The Norman invasion of Malta occurred in 1091, leading to the re-Christianization of the islands. This event initiated the process of latinisation of the Maltese language, setting it on a path of independent evolution from Classical Arabic.",
      "date": "1091"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independent Evolution of Maltese",
      "text": "Following the Norman invasion, Maltese began to evolve independently of Classical Arabic. This process involved significant latinisation, distinguishing Maltese from other Arabic dialects.",
      "date": "1091"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Recognition as National Language",
      "text": "Maltese is recognized as the national language of Malta. It is the only official Semitic and Afroasiatic language of the European Union.",
      "date": "1964"
    }
