      "headline": "First Military Crackdown Begins",
      "text": "The first phase of the military crackdown against the Rohingya people began in October 2016. This operation was characterized by widespread violence, including killings, rapes, and arson, leading to significant displacement of the Rohingya population.",
      "date": "2016-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of First Military Crackdown",
      "text": "The first phase of the military crackdown ended in January 2017. During this period, thousands of Rohingya were forced to flee their homes due to the violence perpetrated by the Myanmar military.",
      "date": "2017-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Military Crackdown Begins",
      "text": "A second, more intense military crackdown against the Rohingya began in August 2017. This phase saw even more severe violence, leading to a massive exodus of Rohingya refugees.",
      "date": "2017-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mass Exodus to Bangladesh",
      "text": "Following the August 2017 crackdown, over 700,000 Rohingya fled to Bangladesh, resulting in the creation of the world's largest refugee camp in Cox's Bazar.",
      "date": "2017-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Recognition of Ethnic Cleansing",
      "text": "Several countries and international organizations began to recognize the events as ethnic cleansing, with calls for accountability and justice for the Rohingya people.",
      "date": "2017"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Court of Justice Case",
      "text": "In November 2019, The Gambia filed a case against Myanmar at the International Court of Justice, accusing it of genocide against the Rohingya people.",
      "date": "2019-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ICJ Orders Myanmar to Protect Rohingya",
      "text": "On January 23, 2020, the International Court of Justice ordered Myanmar to take measures to protect the Rohingya from genocide.",
      "date": "2020-01-23"
    }
  ]
}

