      "headline": "Composition of the Book of Tobit",
      "text": "The Book of Tobit is believed to have been composed around 200 BCE. It is part of the biblical apocrypha and tells the story of Tobit, a righteous Israelite of the tribe of Naphtali.",
      "date": "-0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Book of Judith",
      "text": "The Book of Judith is thought to have been written around 150 BCE. It is a deuterocanonical book, included in the Septuagint and the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox Christian Old Testament.",
      "date": "-0150"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Wisdom of Solomon",
      "text": "The Wisdom of Solomon, also known as the Book of Wisdom, is believed to have been composed around 50 BCE. It is included in the biblical apocrypha and is considered canonical by the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox churches.",
      "date": "-0050"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Book of Sirach",
      "text": "The Book of Sirach, also known as Ecclesiasticus, was written by Ben Sira around 180 BCE. It is included in the biblical apocrypha and is part of the deuterocanonical books.",
      "date": "-0180"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the First Book of Maccabees",
      "text": "The First Book of Maccabees was written around 110 BCE. It is part of the biblical apocrypha and provides a historical account of the Maccabean Revolt.",
      "date": "-0110"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Second Book of Maccabees",
      "text": "The Second Book of Maccabees was composed around 124 BCE. It is part of the biblical apocrypha and focuses on the Jewish revolt against Antiochus IV Epiphanes.",
      "date": "-0124"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Book of Baruch",
      "text": "The Book of Baruch is believed to have been composed around 100 BCE. It is included in the biblical apocrypha and is considered canonical by the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox churches.",
      "date": "-0100"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Letter of Jeremiah",
      "text": "The Letter of Jeremiah, often considered a separate book, is thought to have been written around 300 BCE. It is included in the biblical apocrypha and is considered canonical by the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox churches.",
      "date": "-0300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Additions to Daniel",
      "text": "The Additions to Daniel, which include the Prayer of Azariah, Susanna, and Bel and the Dragon, are believed to have been composed around 100 BCE. They are part of the biblical apocrypha.",
      "date": "-0100"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composition of the Additions to Esther",
      "text": "The Additions to Esther were likely composed around 114 BCE. These additions are part of the biblical apocrypha and are included in the Septuagint.",
