      "headline": "First Ascent of the Matterhorn",
      "text": "The first successful ascent of the Matterhorn was achieved on July 14, 1865, by a team led by Edward Whymper. The ascent was made via the Hörnli ridge, and it marked a significant achievement in the history of mountaineering.",
      "date": "1865-07-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tragic Descent",
      "text": "During the descent of the first ascent on July 14, 1865, four members of the climbing party fell to their deaths. This tragic event cast a shadow over the successful ascent.",
      "date": "1865-07-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Ascent via the Italian Ridge",
      "text": "The first ascent via the Italian (Lion) ridge was completed on July 17, 1865, by Jean-Antoine Carrel and Jean-Baptiste Bich. This route is on the south side of the mountain.",
      "date": "1865-07-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Winter Ascent",
      "text": "The first winter ascent of the Matterhorn was accomplished on March 31, 1876, by J. A. Carrel, J. B. Bich, and A. Meynet.",
      "date": "1876-03-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Ascent of the North Face",
      "text": "The north face of the Matterhorn, one of the great north faces of the Alps, was first climbed on July 31, 1931, by Franz and Toni Schmid.",
      "date": "1931-07-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Ascent of the West Face",
      "text": "The west face of the Matterhorn was first ascended on August 13, 1962, by Renato Daguin and Giovanni Ottin.",
      "date": "1962-08-13"
    }
  ]
}

