      "text": "In 1970, the World Chess Federation (FIDE) adopted the Elo rating system for international chess competitions, further cementing its status as the standard rating system in chess.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Online Chess Ratings",
      "text": "With the advent of online chess platforms, various adaptations of the Elo rating system were implemented to rate players in online games. Popular platforms like Chess.com and Lichess use these systems to provide real-time ratings.",
      "date": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion to Other Games and Contexts",
      "text": "The Elo rating system and its variants have been adopted in other games such as Go, online competitive gaming, and even non-gaming contexts like dating apps, showcasing its versatility and effectiveness in ranking competitive skills.",
      "date": "2000s"
    }
  ]
}

