      "headline": "Publication of The Chymical Wedding of Christian Rosenkreutz",
      "text": "In 1617, the third Rosicrucian manifesto, 'The Chymical Wedding of Christian Rosenkreutz', was published. This allegorical story describes the journey of Christian Rosenkreutz, the legendary founder of the Rosicrucian Order, to a mysterious castle where a royal wedding is taking place.",
      "date": "1617"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of the Order of the Golden and Rosy Cross",
      "text": "In the 1750s, the Order of the Golden and Rosy Cross was founded in Germany. This was a Rosicrucian order that combined elements of alchemy and Kabbalah.",
      "date": "1750"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of the Societas Rosicruciana in Anglia",
      "text": "In 1865, the Societas Rosicruciana in Anglia was founded in England. This society was open only to Master Masons and sought to study the esoteric and mystical aspects of Rosicrucianism.",
      "date": "1865"
