      "headline": "Introduction of the Remington No. 2",
      "text": "The Remington No. 2 typewriter was introduced, which included the QWERTY layout and was the first typewriter to include both upper and lower case letters via a shift key. This model's success helped popularize the QWERTY layout.",
      "date": "1878"
    },
    {
      "headline": "QWERTY Becomes Standard",
      "text": "By the late 19th century, the QWERTY layout became the standard for typewriters and later for computer keyboards, due to its widespread adoption and the success of the Remington typewriters.",
      "date": "1890"
    }
  ]
}

