      "text": "In 313, the Edict of Milan was issued by Constantine the Great and Licinius, proclaiming religious tolerance in the Roman Empire. This marked a significant step towards the separation of church and state.",
      "date": "0313"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peace of Augsburg",
      "text": "In 1555, the Peace of Augsburg was signed, allowing rulers within the Holy Roman Empire to choose either Lutheranism or Catholicism as their realm's official religion, an early form of religious neutrality.",
      "date": "1555"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Westphalia",
      "text": "In 1648, the Treaty of Westphalia ended the Thirty Years' War in Europe and established the principle of state sovereignty over religious affairs, laying groundwork for modern secularism.",
