      "text": "In 1894, Debussy composed 'Prélude à l'après-midi d'un faune', which became one of his most famous orchestral works.",
      "date": "1894"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Premiere of 'Pelléas et Mélisande'",
      "text": "Debussy's opera 'Pelléas et Mélisande' premiered at the Opéra-Comique in Paris on April 30, 1902.",
      "date": "1902-04-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composes 'La Mer'",
      "text": "In 1905, Debussy completed 'La Mer', a symphonic work that is considered one of his masterpieces.",
      "date": "1905"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composes 'Children's Corner'",
      "text": "In 1908, Debussy composed 'Children's Corner', a suite for solo piano dedicated to his daughter, Claude-Emma.",
      "date": "1908"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composes 'Préludes, Book 1'",
      "text": "In 1910, Debussy published 'Préludes, Book 1', a collection of piano pieces that are among his most popular works.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Composes 'Préludes, Book 2'",
      "text": "In 1913, Debussy published 'Préludes, Book 2', continuing his exploration of impressionistic piano music.",
      "date": "1913"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Claude Debussy",
      "text": "Claude Debussy died on March 25, 1918, in Paris, France, during the German bombardment of the city in World War I.",
