      "text": "Antioch on the Orontes was founded by Seleucus I Nicator in 300 BC. It became one of the most important Greek cities of the Hellenistic period.",
      "date": "-0300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capital of the Seleucid Empire",
      "text": "Antioch served as the capital of the Seleucid Empire, playing a central role in the administration and culture of the Hellenistic world.",
      "date": "-0300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Rule",
      "text": "Antioch became a regional capital under Roman rule, continuing its significance as a major city in the Roman Empire.",
      "date": "064"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Byzantine Era",
      "text": "Antioch remained an important city during the Byzantine Empire, serving as a key center of administration and culture.",
      "date": "395"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conquest by the Rashidun Caliphate",
      "text": "In 637, Antioch was conquered by the Rashidun Caliphate, marking the beginning of Islamic rule in the region.",
      "date": "637"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crusader Capture",
      "text": "During the First Crusade, Antioch was captured by the Crusaders in 1098, becoming the capital of the Principality of Antioch.",
