      "headline": "Release of GIF",
      "text": "The Graphics Interchange Format (GIF) was officially released on June 15, 1987.",
      "date": "1987-06-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of GIF89a",
      "text": "In 1989, CompuServe released an enhanced version of the format, called GIF89a, which added support for animation delays, transparent backgrounds, and storage of metadata.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Unisys Patent Controversy",
      "text": "In 1994, Unisys, which held a patent on the LZW compression algorithm used in GIFs, began enforcing licensing fees, leading to controversy and the development of alternative formats.",
      "date": "1994"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expiration of LZW Patent",
      "text": "The patent on the LZW compression algorithm used in GIFs expired in the United States on June 20, 2003, and in Canada on July 7, 2004, allowing for free use of the GIF format.",
      "date": "2003-06-20"
    }
  ]
}

