      "headline": "Founding of Harley-Davidson",
      "text": "Harley-Davidson was founded in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, in 1903 by William S. Harley and Arthur Davidson. The company began with the creation of a small engine designed to fit into a bicycle frame.",
      "date": "1903"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Factory",
      "text": "In 1906, Harley-Davidson built its first factory on Chestnut Street, which is now Juneau Avenue, in Milwaukee. The factory measured 28 by 80 feet.",
      "date": "1906"
