      "text": "In 1909, Harley-Davidson introduced its first V-twin engine, which became a defining feature of the brand's motorcycles.",
      "date": "1909"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Surviving the Great Depression",
      "text": "Harley-Davidson was one of only two American motorcycle manufacturers to survive the Great Depression, continuing operations throughout the 1930s.",
      "date": "1930s"
