      "headline": "Reargument of Brown v. Board of Education",
      "text": "The case was reargued before the Supreme Court on December 8, 1953, after the Court requested further arguments on the issue of whether the Fourteenth Amendment's Equal Protection Clause prohibited the operation of separate public schools for whites and blacks.",
      "date": "1953-12-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Brown v. Board of Education Decision",
      "text": "On May 17, 1954, the U.S. Supreme Court delivered its unanimous decision in Brown v. Board of Education, declaring that racial segregation in public schools was unconstitutional.",
      "date": "1954-05-17"
