      "headline": "Birth of Hasan",
      "text": "Fatima gave birth to her first son, Hasan, in 625 CE. Hasan would later become the second Shia Imam.",
      "date": "0625"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Birth of Husayn",
      "text": "In 626 CE, Fatima gave birth to her second son, Husayn, who would become the third Shia Imam and a central figure in Islamic history.",
      "date": "0626"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Prophet Muhammad",
      "text": "In 632 CE, Fatima's father, Prophet Muhammad, passed away. This event had a profound impact on Fatima and the Muslim community.",
      "date": "0632"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fatima's Dispute Over Inheritance",
      "text": "Following the death of her father in 632 CE, Fatima had a dispute with the first caliph, Abu Bakr, over her inheritance, particularly the land of Fadak.",
      "date": "0632"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Fatima",
      "text": "Fatima passed away in Medina, present-day Saudi Arabia, in 632 CE, just a few months after the death of her father. Her exact date of death is debated, but it is generally believed to have occurred within six months of Muhammad's passing.",
      "date": "0632"
    }
  ]
}

