      "text": "In 1861, Eliot released 'Silas Marner', a novel that tells the story of a reclusive weaver whose life is transformed by the arrival of an orphaned child.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Romola'",
      "text": "Between 1862 and 1863, George Eliot published 'Romola', a historical novel set in 15th-century Florence, exploring themes of political and personal transformation.",
      "date": "1862"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Felix Holt, the Radical'",
      "text": "In 1866, Eliot published 'Felix Holt, the Radical', a novel that addresses political reform and social issues in 19th-century England.",
      "date": "1866"
    },
