      "headline": "AES Competition Announcement",
      "text": "NIST announced a formal call for algorithms for the AES competition on September 12, 1997.",
      "date": "1997-09-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Finalists Announcement",
      "text": "NIST announced the five finalists for the AES competition on August 9, 1999. The finalists were MARS, RC6, Rijndael, Serpent, and Twofish.",
      "date": "1999-08-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "AES Standardization Process",
      "text": "The AES standardization process involved public evaluation and analysis of the candidate algorithms, which took place from 1997 to 2000.",
