      "text": "The Franks emerged as a Germanic tribe living north and east of the Lower Rhine, the Roman border, during the late Roman Empire period.",
      "date": "-00300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Frankish Confederation",
      "text": "By the 3rd century, the Franks had formed a confederation of tribes, including the Salians and the Ripuarians.",
      "date": "0300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Salian Franks Settle in Roman Territory",
      "text": "In 358, the Salian Franks were allowed by the Roman Empire to settle in Toxandria, a region in the Roman province of Germania Inferior.",
      "date": "0358"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Clovis I Becomes King",
      "text": "In 481, Clovis I became king of the Salian Franks and began uniting the Frankish tribes under his rule.",
      "date": "0481"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Soissons",
      "text": "In 486, Clovis I defeated the Roman ruler Syagrius at the Battle of Soissons, expanding Frankish territory.",
      "date": "0486"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conversion to Christianity",
      "text": "Around 496, Clovis I converted to Christianity, which helped to unify the Frankish tribes and gain the support of the Roman Catholic Church.",
      "date": "0496"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Vouillé",
      "text": "In 507, Clovis I defeated the Visigoths at the Battle of Vouillé, further expanding Frankish control into southern Gaul.",
      "date": "0507"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Clovis I",
      "text": "Clovis I died in 511, and his kingdom was divided among his four sons, marking the beginning of the Merovingian dynasty.",
      "date": "0511"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rise of the Carolingians",
      "text": "In the 8th century, the Carolingian family rose to power, eventually replacing the Merovingians as rulers of the Frankish kingdom.",
      "date": "0700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Charlemagne Crowned Emperor",
      "text": "On December 25, 800, Charlemagne was crowned Emperor of the Romans by Pope Leo III, marking the height of Frankish power.",
      "date": "0800-12-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Verdun",
      "text": "In 843, the Treaty of Verdun divided the Carolingian Empire among the three grandsons of Charlemagne, leading to the formation of distinct European kingdoms.",
      "date": "0843"
    }
  ]
}

