      "headline": "Adoption of the North German Confederation Treaty",
      "text": "The process of German unification commenced on 18 August 1866 with the adoption of the North German Confederation Treaty. This treaty established the North German Confederation, initially a military alliance dominated by Prussia.",
      "date": "1866-08-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Austro-Prussian War",
      "text": "The Austro-Prussian War, also known as the Seven Weeks' War, was fought in 1866 between the Austrian Empire and Prussia, with each supported by various allies. The war resulted in Prussian dominance over the German states.",
      "date": "1866"
    },
    {
      "headline": "North German Constitution Adopted",
      "text": "The North German Constitution was adopted on 1 July 1867, further deepening the integration of the North German Confederation under Prussian leadership.",
      "date": "1867-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Franco-Prussian War",
      "text": "The Franco-Prussian War occurred from 19 July 1870 to 28 January 1871. It was a conflict between the Second French Empire and the North German Confederation led by the Kingdom of Prussia. The war ended with a decisive German victory.",
      "date": "1870-07-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Proclamation of the German Empire",
      "text": "On 18 January 1871, the German Empire was proclaimed in the Hall of Mirrors at the Palace of Versailles. King Wilhelm I of Prussia was declared the German Emperor, marking the unification of Germany.",
      "date": "1871-01-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Frankfurt",
      "text": "The Treaty of Frankfurt was signed on 10 May 1871, officially ending the Franco-Prussian War. It resulted in territorial gains for the newly unified Germany, including Alsace and parts of Lorraine.",
      "date": "1871-05-10"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
