      "text": "In 1976, Whitfield Diffie and Martin Hellman published the Diffie-Hellman key exchange method. This was a groundbreaking development in the field of cryptography, as it introduced the concept of public key cryptography, allowing two parties to securely generate a shared secret over a public channel.",
