      "headline": "Birth of Oedipus",
      "text": "Oedipus was born to King Laius and Queen Jocasta of Thebes. According to prophecy, he was destined to kill his father and marry his mother.",
      "date": "-1250"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abandonment on Mount Cithaeron",
      "text": "Shortly after his birth, Oedipus was abandoned on Mount Cithaeron by his parents to avoid the prophecy. He was left with his feet bound.",
      "date": "-1249"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption by King Polybus and Queen Merope",
      "text": "Oedipus was found and adopted by King Polybus and Queen Merope of Corinth, who raised him as their own son.",
      "date": "-1248"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Consultation with the Oracle of Delphi",
      "text": "As a young man, Oedipus visited the Oracle of Delphi, who told him he was destined to kill his father and marry his mother.",
      "date": "-1230"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Killing of King Laius",
      "text": "On his way to Thebes, Oedipus encountered and killed a man at a crossroads, who was later revealed to be his biological father, King Laius.",
      "date": "-1225"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Solving the Riddle of the Sphinx",
      "text": "Oedipus solved the riddle of the Sphinx, freeing Thebes from its curse and was made king as a reward.",
      "date": "-1225"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Queen Jocasta",
      "text": "Oedipus married the widowed Queen Jocasta, unaware that she was his biological mother.",
      "date": "-1225"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of the Truth",
      "text": "Years later, the truth of Oedipus's parentage and his actions were revealed, leading to Jocasta's suicide and Oedipus's self-inflicted blindness.",
      "date": "-1210"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile from Thebes",
      "text": "Following the revelation of his actions, Oedipus was exiled from Thebes and wandered as a blind beggar.",
      "date": "-1205"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Oedipus",
      "text": "Oedipus died at Colonus, where he was said to have been taken by the gods, bringing peace to the land.",
      "date": "-1200"
    }
  ]
}

