      "text": "In January 2016, astronomers Konstantin Batygin and Michael E. Brown proposed the existence of a hypothetical ninth planet in the outer region of the Solar System. This planet, referred to as Planet Nine, was suggested to explain the peculiar clustering of orbits for a group of extreme trans-Neptunian objects (ETNOs).",
