      "headline": "Enunciation of the Lost Cause",
      "text": "The Lost Cause of the Confederacy was first enunciated in 1866. It emerged as a pseudohistorical and historical negationist myth that argued the Confederate cause during the American Civil War was just and heroic, and not centered on slavery.",
      "date": "1866"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Influence on Southern United States",
      "text": "The Lost Cause myth continued to influence racism, gender roles, and religious attitudes in the Southern United States into the 21st century.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Historians Dismantle the Myth",
      "text": "Historians have dismantled many parts of the Lost Cause mythos, highlighting its inaccuracies and the ways it has been used to justify racism and other social issues.",
      "date": "2023"
    }
  ]
}

