      "headline": "Formation of the Patriotic Front",
      "text": "In 1976, the Zimbabwe African National Union (ZANU) and the Zimbabwe African People's Union (ZAPU) formed an alliance known as the Patriotic Front to strengthen their efforts against the Rhodesian government.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lancaster House Agreement",
      "text": "The Lancaster House Agreement was signed on December 21, 1979, marking the end of the Rhodesian Bush War. It led to the establishment of a ceasefire and paved the way for the transition to majority rule.",
      "date": "1979-12-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Rhodesian Bush War",
      "text": "The Rhodesian Bush War officially ended in December 1979 following the signing of the Lancaster House Agreement.",
      "date": "1979-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence of Zimbabwe",
      "text": "On April 18, 1980, Zimbabwe officially gained independence from British colonial rule, marking the end of the transition period following the Rhodesian Bush War.",
      "date": "1980-04-18"
    }
  ]
}

