      "text": "The idea for the Voyager Golden Record was conceived as part of the Voyager program, which aimed to send spacecraft to explore the outer planets. The concept was to create a time capsule that would communicate the story of our world to extraterrestrials.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Selection of Content for the Golden Record",
      "text": "A committee chaired by Carl Sagan was formed to select the content for the Voyager Golden Record. The committee included scientists, artists, and musicians who curated a collection of sounds and images that represent the diversity of life and culture on Earth.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Voyager Golden Record",
      "text": "The Voyager Golden Record was completed, containing 115 images and a variety of natural sounds, such as those made by surf, wind, and thunder, as well as animal sounds, including the songs of birds and whales. It also included musical selections from different cultures and eras, spoken greetings in 55 languages, and printed messages from President Jimmy Carter and U.N. Secretary-General Kurt Waldheim.",
      "date": "1977"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of Voyager 2",
      "text": "Voyager 2 was launched on August 20, 1977, carrying one of the two identical Golden Records.",
      "date": "1977-08-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of Voyager 1",
      "text": "Voyager 1 was launched on September 5, 1977, carrying the second of the two identical Golden Records.",
      "date": "1977-09-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 1 Exits the Solar System",
