      "headline": "Origins of House Music",
      "text": "House music originated in the early 1980s in Chicago, Illinois. It was created by DJs and music producers from Chicago's underground club culture, which consisted of Black gay men. They began altering disco songs to give them a more mechanical beat.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First House Music Record",
      "text": "In 1984, Jesse Saunders released 'On & On', which is considered the first house music record. This track played a significant role in defining the genre.",
