      "headline": "Foundation of Bata Corporation",
      "text": "Bata Corporation was founded on August 24, 1894, in Zlín, Moravia, which is now part of the Czech Republic, by Tomáš Baťa, his brother Antonín, and his sister Anna.",
      "date": "1894-08-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Mass Production",
      "text": "In 1904, Tomáš Baťa visited the United States and was inspired by the mass production techniques used in the shoe industry there. Upon his return, he implemented these techniques in Bata's operations.",
      "date": "1904"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion During World War I",
      "text": "During World War I, Bata Corporation expanded significantly due to increased demand for military shoes. By 1917, the company employed over 5,000 people.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Bata's Own Town",
      "text": "In 1923, the company began developing its own town, Baťov, later known as Zlín, which included housing, schools, and other facilities for its workers.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Tomáš Baťa",
      "text": "Tomáš Baťa died in a plane crash on July 12, 1932. His half-brother Jan Antonín Baťa took over the leadership of the company.",
      "date": "1932-07-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Global Expansion",
      "text": "By the late 1930s, Bata had expanded globally, with factories in over 30 countries and sales in more than 50 countries.",
      "date": "1930s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nationalization in Czechoslovakia",
      "text": "After World War II, in 1945, the Czechoslovak government nationalized Bata's assets in the country.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Relocation of Headquarters",
      "text": "In 1964, Bata moved its headquarters to Toronto, Canada, as part of its strategy to focus on international markets.",
      "date": "1964"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Czech Republic",
      "text": "In the 1990s, after the fall of communism, Bata returned to the Czech Republic and re-established its presence there.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Headquarters Moved to Lausanne",
      "text": "In 2004, Bata moved its global headquarters to Lausanne, Switzerland, to better manage its international operations.",
      "date": "2004"
    }
  ]
}

