      "headline": "Akkadian as the Lingua Franca",
      "text": "During the Akkadian Empire (circa 2334–2154 BCE), Akkadian became the lingua franca of Mesopotamia and the Near East.",
      "date": "-02334"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Old Akkadian Period",
      "text": "The Old Akkadian period is characterized by the use of Akkadian in inscriptions and administrative documents from around 2500 BCE to 2000 BCE.",
