      "text": "Nanjing was the capital of the Southern Dynasties, including Liu Song, Southern Qi, Liang, and Chen, from 420 to 589.",
      "date": "0420"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capital of the Southern Tang",
      "text": "During the Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period, Nanjing was the capital of the Southern Tang from 937 to 975.",
      "date": "0937"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ming Dynasty Capital",
      "text": "Nanjing became the capital of the Ming dynasty in 1368, serving as the primary capital until 1421.",
      "date": "1368"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Taiping Heavenly Kingdom",
      "text": "Nanjing was the capital of the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom from 1853 to 1864 during the Taiping Rebellion.",
      "date": "1853"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Republic of China Capital",
      "text": "Nanjing was declared the capital of the Republic of China in 1927 and served as the capital until 1949.",
      "date": "1927"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nanjing Massacre",
      "text": "The Nanjing Massacre occurred from December 1937 to January 1938, during which Japanese troops killed and assaulted numerous civilians.",
      "date": "1937-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capital Relocation",
      "text": "In 1949, the capital of the People's Republic of China was moved from Nanjing to Beijing.",
      "date": "1949"
    },
    {
      "headline": "UN Habitat Scroll of Honor",
      "text": "In 2008, Nanjing was awarded the Habitat Scroll of Honor by the United Nations.",
