    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty with Muawiya",
      "text": "In August 661, Hasan ibn Ali signed a treaty with Muawiya, abdicating his claim to the caliphate in exchange for peace and certain conditions, effectively ending his brief rule as caliph.",
      "date": "0661-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Hasan ibn Ali",
      "text": "Hasan ibn Ali died in Medina in April 670. It is widely believed that he was poisoned, possibly at the instigation of the Umayyad caliph Muawiya.",
