      "text": "The Gospel of Matthew is believed to have been composed between 80 and 90 AD. It is the first book of the New Testament and one of the three synoptic Gospels.",
      "date": "0080"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Content and Themes",
      "text": "The Gospel of Matthew tells how Israel's messiah, Jesus, comes to his people but is rejected by them. After his resurrection, Jesus sends the disciples to the gentiles instead. The gospel emphasizes the importance of Jewish tradition in a church increasingly becoming gentile.",
      "date": "0080"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Criticism of Scribes and Pharisees",
      "text": "The Gospel of Matthew includes sharp criticism of the scribes and Pharisees, reflecting the struggles and conflicts between the evangelist's community and other Jews.",
      "date": "0080"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Transfer of the Kingdom of Heaven",
      "text": "According to the Gospel of Matthew, through the rejection of Christ by the scribes and Pharisees, the Kingdom of Heaven has been taken away from them and given to the church.",
      "date": "0080"
    }
  ]
}

