      "headline": "Centennial Olympic Park Bombing",
      "text": "On July 27, 1996, a domestic terrorist pipe bombing attack occurred at Centennial Olympic Park in Atlanta, Georgia, during the Summer Olympics. The blast directly killed one person and injured 111 others; another person later died of a heart attack.",
      "date": "1996-07-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of the Bomb",
      "text": "Security guard Richard Jewell discovered the bomb before detonation, notified Georgia Bureau of Investigation officers, and began clearing spectators out of the park along with other security guards.",
      "date": "1996-07-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eric Rudolph's Terrorism Campaign",
      "text": "The Centennial Olympic Park bombing was the first of four bombings committed by Eric Rudolph in a terrorism campaign against the U.S. government, which he accused of championing 'the ideals of global socialism' and 'abortion on demand'.",
      "date": "1996"
    }
  ]
