      "text": "The Selective Service System was established in 1917 to manage the conscription of U.S. citizens for military service during World War I.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Selective Training and Service Act of 1940",
      "text": "The Selective Training and Service Act of 1940 was enacted, establishing the first peacetime draft in U.S. history and requiring men between the ages of 21 and 35 to register with the Selective Service.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II Draft",
      "text": "During World War II, the Selective Service System was responsible for drafting millions of men into military service.",
      "date": "1941"
