      "headline": "County of Flanders Established",
      "text": "The County of Flanders was established in the 9th century as a feudal fief in the Kingdom of West Francia. It became one of the most powerful principalities in the region.",
      "date": "0875"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of the Golden Spurs",
      "text": "On July 11, 1302, the Battle of the Golden Spurs took place near Kortrijk. Flemish forces defeated the French army, marking a significant victory for the County of Flanders.",
      "date": "1302-07-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Flanders under Burgundian Rule",
      "text": "In 1384, the County of Flanders came under the control of the Duchy of Burgundy through the marriage of Margaret III of Flanders to Philip the Bold.",
      "date": "1384"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Flanders Becomes Part of the Habsburg Netherlands",
      "text": "In 1482, following the death of Mary of Burgundy, Flanders became part of the Habsburg Netherlands under the rule of Maximilian I.",
      "date": "1482"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Rule in Flanders",
      "text": "The Treaty of Cateau-Cambrésis in 1559 confirmed Spanish control over Flanders, which became part of the Spanish Netherlands.",
      "date": "1559"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Flanders Under Austrian Rule",
      "text": "In 1713, the Treaty of Utrecht transferred control of Flanders from Spain to Austria, marking the beginning of Austrian rule.",
      "date": "1713"
    },
    {
      "headline": "French Annexation of Flanders",
      "text": "In 1795, during the French Revolutionary Wars, Flanders was annexed by the French Republic and became part of France.",
      "date": "1795"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Flanders Becomes Part of the United Kingdom of the Netherlands",
      "text": "Following the defeat of Napoleon, the Congress of Vienna in 1815 established the United Kingdom of the Netherlands, which included Flanders.",
      "date": "1815"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Belgian Revolution",
      "text": "In 1830, the Belgian Revolution led to the independence of Belgium from the United Kingdom of the Netherlands, with Flanders becoming part of the new Belgian state.",
      "date": "1830"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Flemish Movement Gains Momentum",
      "text": "In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, the Flemish Movement gained momentum, advocating for the recognition of Dutch as an official language in Belgium.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Flemish Community Established",
      "text": "In 1980, the Flemish Community was officially established as part of the federalization of Belgium, granting cultural autonomy to Flanders.",
