      "text": "By the 19th century, the ampersand was included as the 27th letter of the English alphabet, often recited as 'and per se and' at the end of the alphabet.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Usage",
      "text": "Today, the ampersand is widely used in various contexts, including business names, logos, and informal writing, representing the word 'and'.",
