      "headline": "Concept of SMS Developed",
      "text": "The concept of SMS was developed in the Franco-German GSM cooperation in 1984 by Friedhelm Hillebrand and Bernard Ghillebaert.",
      "date": "1984"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First SMS Sent",
      "text": "The first SMS message was sent on December 3, 1992, by Neil Papworth, a test engineer for Sema Group, from a personal computer to Richard Jarvis of Vodafone using the Vodafone GSM network in the United Kingdom. The message read 'Merry Christmas'.",
      "date": "1992-12-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "SMS Commercially Available",
      "text": "SMS became commercially available to the public in 1993, when Nokia introduced the first mobile phone that supported user-written SMS text messages.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of T9 Predictive Text",
      "text": "In 1995, Tegic Communications introduced T9, a predictive text technology that made it easier to compose SMS messages on mobile phones.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "SMS Gaining Popularity",
      "text": "By the late 1990s, SMS began to gain popularity, especially among young people, as a quick and convenient way to communicate.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "SMS Interoperability",
      "text": "In 1999, SMS interoperability between different networks was introduced, allowing users to send messages across different mobile networks.",
      "date": "1999"
    },
    {
      "headline": "SMS Becomes a Global Phenomenon",
      "text": "By the early 2000s, SMS had become a global phenomenon, with billions of messages being sent annually worldwide.",
      "date": "2000s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peak of SMS Usage",
      "text": "SMS usage peaked in the early 2010s, with trillions of messages sent each year globally.",
      "date": "2010s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline in SMS Usage",
      "text": "With the rise of internet-based messaging apps like WhatsApp and Facebook Messenger, SMS usage began to decline in the mid-2010s.",
      "date": "2010s"
    }
  ]
}

