      "headline": "Introduction of CAPTCHA",
      "text": "The term CAPTCHA was coined in 2000 by Luis von Ahn, Manuel Blum, Nicholas J. Hopper, and John Langford of Carnegie Mellon University. It stands for 'Completely Automated Public Turing test to tell Computers and Humans Apart'.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Use of CAPTCHA",
      "text": "The first use of CAPTCHA was implemented by Yahoo to prevent bots from creating accounts on their platform.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "reCAPTCHA Development",
      "text": "In 2007, Luis von Ahn and his team developed reCAPTCHA, a system that uses CAPTCHA challenges to digitize books and improve machine learning.",
      "date": "2007"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Google Acquires reCAPTCHA",
      "text": "In 2009, Google acquired reCAPTCHA to help digitize books and improve its optical character recognition technology.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of No CAPTCHA reCAPTCHA",
      "text": "In 2014, Google introduced 'No CAPTCHA reCAPTCHA', which allowed users to verify themselves as human with a single click, improving user experience.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of reCAPTCHA v3",
      "text": "In 2018, Google launched reCAPTCHA v3, which provides a score based on user interactions to determine if the user is human, eliminating the need for user interaction.",
      "date": "2018"
    }
  ]
}

