      "text": "In 1984, hooks published 'Feminist Theory: From Margin to Center', where she critiqued the feminist movement for its lack of inclusivity.",
      "date": "1984"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Talking Back: Thinking Feminist, Thinking Black'",
      "text": "In 1989, hooks released 'Talking Back: Thinking Feminist, Thinking Black', a collection of essays exploring feminist theory and race.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Yearning: Race, Gender, and Cultural Politics'",
      "text": "In 1990, hooks published 'Yearning: Race, Gender, and Cultural Politics', which further explored the intersections of race, gender, and culture.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Teaching to Transgress: Education as the Practice of Freedom'",
      "text": "In 1994, hooks published 'Teaching to Transgress: Education as the Practice of Freedom', discussing education as a means of liberation.",
      "date": "1994"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'All About Love: New Visions'",
      "text": "In 2000, hooks published 'All About Love: New Visions', where she examined the concept of love in modern society.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Distinguished Professor in Residence at Berea College",
      "text": "bell hooks became a Distinguished Professor in Residence at Berea College in Kentucky, where she continued her work in education and social critique.",
      "date": "2004"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of bell hooks",
      "text": "bell hooks passed away on December 15, 2021, at her home in Berea, Kentucky, at the age of 69.",
      "date": "2021-12-15"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
