      "text": "Max Born completed his habilitation, a qualification for university teaching, at the University of Göttingen in 1909.",
      "date": "1909"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Professorship at the University of Göttingen",
      "text": "In 1921, Max Born was appointed as a professor of theoretical physics at the University of Göttingen.",
      "date": "1921"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Quantum Mechanics",
      "text": "During the 1920s, Max Born made significant contributions to the development of quantum mechanics, including the statistical interpretation of the wave function.",
      "date": "1920"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nobel Prize in Physics",
      "text": "Max Born was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1954 for his fundamental research in quantum mechanics, especially in the statistical interpretation of the wave function.",
      "date": "1954"
