      "headline": "Pakistan's Surrender in Dhaka",
      "text": "On 16 December 1971, the Eastern Command of the Pakistan military signed the instrument of surrender in Dhaka, leading to the formation of East Pakistan as the new nation of Bangladesh.",
      "date": "1971-12-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prisoners of War",
      "text": "Approximately 93,000 Pakistani servicemen were taken prisoner by the Indian Army after the surrender on 16 December 1971. This included 79,676 to 81,000 uniformed personnel of the Pakistan Armed Forces and 10,324 to 12,500 civilians.",
      "date": "1971-12-16"
    }
  ]
}

