      "headline": "Earliest Known Reference to Eye Surgery",
      "text": "The earliest known reference to eye surgery is found in the Code of Hammurabi, dating back to around 1754 BCE, which mentions fees for eye surgery.",
      "date": "-1754"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sushruta's Contributions",
      "text": "Sushruta, an ancient Indian surgeon, described cataract surgery in his work, the Sushruta Samhita, around 600 BCE.",
      "date": "-0600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Galen's Work on the Eye",
      "text": "In the 2nd century CE, the Greek physician Galen made significant contributions to the understanding of the anatomy and physiology of the eye.",
      "date": "0150"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alhazen's Book of Optics",
      "text": "In the early 11th century, the Arab scientist Alhazen wrote the Book of Optics, which laid the foundation for the study of optics and vision.",
