      "headline": "Disappearance of Malaysia Airlines Flight 370",
      "text": "On 2014-03-08, Malaysia Airlines Flight 370 disappeared after departing from Kuala Lumpur for Beijing. The aircraft had 227 passengers and 12 crew members on board.",
      "date": "2014-03-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Official Statement by Malaysian Prime Minister",
      "text": "On 2014-03-24, Malaysia's then Prime Minister, Najib Razak, announced that the aircraft's flight ended somewhere in the Indian Ocean. However, no further explanation was provided at the time.",
      "date": "2014-03-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Discovery of Debris",
      "text": "In July 2015, a piece of debris was found on Réunion Island, which was later confirmed to be from Malaysia Airlines Flight 370. This was the first piece of physical evidence that the aircraft had crashed.",
      "date": "2015-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Criticism and Theories",
      "text": "Following the disappearance and official announcements, many critics questioned the explanations provided. Several theories about the disappearance were proposed, some of which were described as conspiracy theories.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
