      "text": "The Kingdom of Wessex was traditionally founded in 519 by Cerdic and Cynric after their victory at the Battle of Cerdicesford.",
      "date": "0519"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Mons Badonicus",
      "text": "Around 500, the Battle of Mons Badonicus was fought, where the Britons, possibly under the command of a leader like Arthur, defeated the Anglo-Saxons, halting their advance for several decades.",
      "date": "0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of King Cædwalla",
      "text": "Cædwalla reigned from 685 to 688 and expanded Wessex's territory significantly, including the conquest of the Isle of Wight.",
      "date": "0685"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of King Ine",
      "text": "King Ine ruled from 688 to 726 and is known for issuing one of the earliest English law codes.",
      "date": "0688"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of King Egbert",
      "text": "Egbert became king in 802 and is credited with uniting much of southern England under his rule by 829, after defeating the Mercians at the Battle of Ellandun in 825.",
      "date": "0802"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Ellandun",
      "text": "In 825, Egbert of Wessex defeated Beornwulf of Mercia at the Battle of Ellandun, leading to the end of Mercian dominance over southern England.",
      "date": "0825"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of King Æthelwulf",
      "text": "Æthelwulf, son of Egbert, reigned from 839 to 858 and is noted for his pilgrimage to Rome and his efforts to defend against Viking invasions.",
      "date": "0839"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of King Alfred the Great",
      "text": "Alfred the Great reigned from 871 to 899 and is renowned for his defense against Viking invasions, his educational reforms, and his legal code.",
      "date": "0871"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Edington",
      "text": "In 878, Alfred the Great defeated the Viking Great Heathen Army at the Battle of Edington, leading to the Treaty of Wedmore and the establishment of Danelaw.",
      "date": "0878"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alfred the Great becomes King of the Anglo-Saxons",
      "text": "In 886, Alfred the Great declared himself King of the Anglo-Saxons, marking the transition from the Kingdom of Wessex to a more unified English kingdom.",
      "date": "0886"
    }
  ]
}

