      "text": "In 1659, the Treaty of the Pyrenees was signed, which affected the territorial boundaries of the Basque Country, dividing it between France and Spain.",
      "date": "1659"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Carlist Wars",
      "text": "The Basque Country was a major battleground during the Carlist Wars in the 19th century, particularly between 1833 and 1876.",
      "date": "1833"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Civil War",
      "text": "During the Spanish Civil War (1936-1939), the Basque Country was a significant site of conflict, with the bombing of Guernica on April 26, 1937, being a notable event.",
      "date": "1937-04-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Statute of Autonomy of the Basque Country",
      "text": "In 1979, the Statute of Autonomy of the Basque Country was approved, granting the Basque Country a degree of self-governance within Spain.",
      "date": "1979"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ETA Ceasefire",
      "text": "On October 20, 2011, the Basque separatist group ETA announced a definitive cessation of its armed activities.",
