      "headline": "Formation of Front for National Salvation (FRONASA)",
      "text": "In 1971, Museveni founded the Front for National Salvation (FRONASA), a rebel group to fight against Idi Amin's regime.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ugandan Bush War",
      "text": "Museveni led the National Resistance Army (NRA) in the Ugandan Bush War from 1981 to 1986, fighting against the government of Milton Obote.",
      "date": "1981"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Becomes President of Uganda",
      "text": "On January 29, 1986, Yoweri Museveni was sworn in as the President of Uganda after his forces captured Kampala.",
      "date": "1986-01-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Structural Adjustment Programs",
      "text": "In the late 1980s, Museveni's government implemented structural adjustment programs with the support of the International Monetary Fund and World Bank.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitutional Reforms",
      "text": "In 1995, a new constitution was adopted in Uganda under Museveni's leadership, which introduced a multi-party political system.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election as President",
      "text": "Museveni was re-elected as President of Uganda in the 1996 elections, the first under the new constitution.",
      "date": "1996"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abolition of Presidential Term Limits",
      "text": "In 2005, the Ugandan parliament voted to abolish presidential term limits, allowing Museveni to run for additional terms.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election in 2011",
      "text": "Museveni was re-elected in the 2011 presidential elections, extending his presidency.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election in 2016",
      "text": "Museveni won the 2016 presidential elections, continuing his long tenure as President of Uganda.",
      "date": "2016"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election in 2021",
      "text": "In January 2021, Museveni was re-elected for another term as President of Uganda.",
      "date": "2021-01"
    }
  ]
}

