      "date": "1993-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ceasefire Agreement",
      "text": "A ceasefire agreement was signed between the Sri Lankan government and the LTTE on February 22, 2002, facilitated by Norway, aiming to bring an end to hostilities.",
      "date": "2002-02-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Resumption of Hostilities",
      "text": "In 2006, hostilities resumed between the Sri Lankan government and the LTTE, leading to a full-scale military offensive by the government.",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Sri Lankan Civil War",
      "text": "The Sri Lankan Civil War officially ended on May 18, 2009, with the defeat of the LTTE and the death of its leader, Velupillai Prabhakaran.",
