      "headline": "Nero Marries Sporus",
      "text": "In 66 CE, the Roman Emperor Nero married Sporus, a young slave boy whom he had castrated. This marriage took place during Nero's tour of Greece. Nero allegedly married Sporus to play the role of his deceased wife, Poppaea Sabina.",
      "date": "0066"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sporus Accompanies Nero",
      "text": "Sporus accompanied Nero on his tour of Greece in 66-67 CE, where he was treated as an empress and participated in public events alongside Nero.",
      "date": "0066"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nero's Death",
      "text": "In June 68 CE, Emperor Nero died by suicide. Following Nero's death, Sporus was taken by Nymphidius Sabinus, who attempted to use him to gain legitimacy as Nero's successor.",
      "date": "0068-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sporus with Otho",
      "text": "After the death of Nymphidius Sabinus, Sporus was taken by Otho, who briefly became emperor in 69 CE. Otho treated Sporus with respect, continuing to regard him as an empress.",
      "date": "0069"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sporus with Vitellius",
      "text": "Following Otho's death, Sporus was taken by Vitellius, who became emperor in 69 CE. Vitellius planned to use Sporus in a public spectacle, but Sporus chose to end his own life to avoid this humiliation.",
      "date": "0069"
    }
  ]
}

