      "headline": "First Civilian Awarded the Victoria Cross",
      "text": "The first and only civilian to be awarded the Victoria Cross was Thomas Kavanagh, who received it in 1858 for his actions during the Indian Mutiny.",
      "date": "1858"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Last Civilian Awarded the Victoria Cross",
      "text": "The last civilian to receive the Victoria Cross was awarded in 1879. Since then, no civilian has been awarded the VC.",
      "date": "1879"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Victoria Cross Awarded Posthumously",
      "text": "The Victoria Cross has been awarded posthumously since its inception, recognizing acts of valor even if the recipient did not survive.",
      "date": "1856"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Victoria Cross in the British Empire",
      "text": "The Victoria Cross was awarded to service personnel throughout the British Empire until many successor independent nations established their own honors systems.",
      "date": "20th century"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Victoria Cross Investitures",
      "text": "Since the first awards, two-thirds of all Victoria Crosses have been personally presented by the British monarch, usually at Buckingham Palace.",
