    {
      "headline": "Origin of Hermes Trismegistus",
      "text": "Hermes Trismegistus is a legendary figure that emerged during the Hellenistic period as a syncretic combination of the Greek god Hermes and the Egyptian god Thoth. The exact date of origin is not specified, but it is associated with the Hellenistic period, which spans from 323 BCE to 31 BCE.",
      "date": "-0323"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Authorship of the Hermetica",
      "text": "Hermes Trismegistus is traditionally credited as the author of the Hermetica, a collection of writings that are considered foundational texts of Hermeticism. These texts were written over several centuries, with the earliest dating back to the 2nd century CE.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Influence on Hermeticism",
      "text": "The writings attributed to Hermes Trismegistus laid the basis for Hermeticism, a philosophical and religious tradition that emerged in the early centuries of the Common Era. Hermeticism has influenced various philosophical systems and esoteric traditions throughout history.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaissance Revival",
      "text": "During the Renaissance, the figure of Hermes Trismegistus and the Hermetic texts experienced a revival. Scholars and thinkers of the time, such as Marsilio Ficino and Giovanni Pico della Mirandola, were influenced by Hermeticism, integrating its ideas into their own works.",
      "date": "1400"
    }
  ]
}

