      "headline": "Creation of the FBI",
      "text": "The FBI was created on July 26, 1908, when Attorney General Charles Bonaparte ordered a group of newly hired federal investigators to report to Chief Examiner Stanley W. Finch of the Department of Justice.",
      "date": "1908-07-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Major Case",
      "text": "In 1910, the FBI handled its first major case, the Mann Act, which involved the transportation of women across state lines for immoral purposes.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "J. Edgar Hoover Becomes Director",
      "text": "On May 10, 1924, J. Edgar Hoover was appointed as the Director of the Bureau of Investigation, which later became the FBI.",
      "date": "1924-05-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming to Federal Bureau of Investigation",
      "text": "In 1935, the Bureau of Investigation was renamed the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI).",
      "date": "1935"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FBI's Role in World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, the FBI was involved in counterintelligence operations and worked to prevent espionage and sabotage within the United States.",
      "date": "1941"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COINTELPRO Initiation",
      "text": "In 1956, the FBI initiated COINTELPRO, a series of covert and often illegal projects aimed at surveilling, infiltrating, discrediting, and disrupting domestic political organizations.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FBI's Involvement in Civil Rights Movement",
      "text": "During the 1960s, the FBI was involved in monitoring civil rights leaders and organizations, including Martin Luther King Jr.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Watergate Investigation",
      "text": "In 1972, the FBI played a crucial role in the investigation of the Watergate scandal, which led to the resignation of President Richard Nixon.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Hostage Rescue Team",
      "text": "In 1982, the FBI established the Hostage Rescue Team (HRT), a full-time counterterrorism unit.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "September 11 Attacks",
      "text": "Following the September 11, 2001, terrorist attacks, the FBI shifted its focus to counterterrorism and national security.",
      "date": "2001-09-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Terrorist Screening Center",
      "text": "In 2003, the FBI established the Terrorist Screening Center to consolidate the government's approach to terrorist screening.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
