    },
    {
      "headline": "EEA Agreement Contracting Parties",
      "text": "The contracting parties of the EEA Agreement are the European Union, its member states, and three of the four EFTA states: Iceland, Liechtenstein, and Norway. The agreement allows these countries to participate in the EU's internal market.",
      "date": "1994-01-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Article 128 of the EEA Agreement",
      "text": "According to Article 128 of the EEA Agreement, any European State becoming a member of the EU shall, and the Swiss Confederation or any European State becoming a member of EFTA may, apply to become a party to the EEA Agreement. This highlights the process for new members to join the EEA.",
      "date": "1994-01-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Schengen and Dublin Agreements",
      "text": "Although Schengen is not a part of the EEA Agreement, all four EFTA States participate in Schengen and Dublin through bilateral agreements. They apply the provisions of the relevant Acquis.",
