      "headline": "First Thru-Hike",
      "text": "Earl Shaffer became the first person to complete a thru-hike of the Appalachian Trail in 1948, hiking from Georgia to Maine.",
      "date": "1948"
    },
    {
      "headline": "National Scenic Trail Designation",
      "text": "The Appalachian Trail was designated as the first National Scenic Trail in 1968 under the National Trails System Act.",
      "date": "1968"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Appalachian Trail Conservancy",
      "text": "The Appalachian Trail Conference was renamed the Appalachian Trail Conservancy in 2005 to better reflect its mission and role.",
