      "headline": "Birth of Draupadi",
      "text": "Draupadi was born out of a sacrificial fire along with her brother Dhrishtadyumna. She was the daughter of King Drupada of Panchala. Her birth is considered divine and miraculous.",
      "date": "-0300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Swayamvara of Draupadi",
      "text": "Draupadi's swayamvara was held, where she was to choose her husband from among the assembled princes. Arjuna, disguised as a Brahmin, won the contest by shooting an arrow through a revolving target.",
      "date": "-0280"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to the Pandavas",
      "text": "Following the swayamvara, Draupadi married all five Pandava brothers: Yudhishthira, Bhima, Arjuna, Nakula, and Sahadeva, as per her mother's inadvertent command.",
      "date": "-0280"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Humiliation at the Kaurava court",
      "text": "Draupadi was humiliated in the Kaurava court after Yudhishthira lost her in a dice game. Dushasana attempted to disrobe her, but she was saved by divine intervention.",
      "date": "-0275"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile with the Pandavas",
      "text": "After the dice game, Draupadi and the Pandavas were exiled for 13 years, including one year in disguise.",
      "date": "-0275"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return from Exile",
      "text": "Draupadi and the Pandavas returned from exile and demanded their kingdom back, leading to the Kurukshetra War.",
      "date": "-0262"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Kurukshetra War",
      "text": "The Kurukshetra War took place, where Draupadi's sons and many other relatives were killed. The Pandavas emerged victorious.",
      "date": "-0262"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Draupadi",
      "text": "Draupadi died during the Pandavas' final journey to the Himalayas, known as the Mahaprasthanika Parva.",
