      "headline": "Filming of the Zapruder Film",
      "text": "On November 22, 1963, Abraham Zapruder filmed the motorcade of United States President John F. Kennedy as it passed through Dealey Plaza in Dallas, Texas. The film unexpectedly captured the assassination of President Kennedy.",
      "date": "1963-11-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Initial Development and Viewing",
      "text": "Shortly after the assassination on November 22, 1963, the Zapruder film was developed at a local Dallas photo lab. Zapruder allowed the film to be viewed by the Secret Service and other officials.",
      "date": "1963-11-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sale of Film Rights to Life Magazine",
      "text": "On November 23, 1963, Abraham Zapruder sold the print rights of the film to Life magazine for $150,000, which was paid in six annual installments.",
      "date": "1963-11-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Life Magazine Publication",
      "text": "Life magazine published individual frames of the Zapruder film in its November 29, 1963, issue, but did not publish the film in its entirety.",
      "date": "1963-11-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Broadcast of the Film",
      "text": "The Zapruder film was first broadcast on television by ABC's 'Good Night America' on March 6, 1975, hosted by Geraldo Rivera.",
      "date": "1975-03-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Government Acquisition",
      "text": "In 1999, the Zapruder film was declared an 'assassination record' and was acquired by the U.S. government for $16 million.",
      "date": "1999"
    }
  ]
}

