      "headline": "Pasteur's Early Research",
      "text": "In the 1850s, Louis Pasteur began his research into fermentation and the role of microorganisms, which laid the groundwork for his later development of pasteurization.",
      "date": "1850"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Pasteurization",
      "text": "In 1864, Louis Pasteur developed the process of pasteurization, which involves heating liquids to a specific temperature to kill harmful microorganisms without affecting the taste or quality of the product.",
      "date": "1864"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Application of Pasteurization",
      "text": "Pasteurization was first applied to wine and beer in the 1860s to prevent spoilage and improve shelf life.",
      "date": "1860"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Pasteurization of Milk",
      "text": "The process of pasteurizing milk was developed in the late 19th century, significantly reducing the incidence of milk-borne diseases.",
      "date": "1880"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Widespread Adoption of Milk Pasteurization",
      "text": "By the early 20th century, pasteurization of milk became widespread in many countries, contributing to public health improvements.",
      "date": "1900"
    }
  ]
}

