      "text": "Messianic Judaism began to emerge in the 19th century as a movement that sought to combine Jewish traditions with belief in Jesus as the Messiah. This period saw the formation of small groups of Jewish believers in Jesus who maintained their Jewish identity while adopting Christian theological views.",
