      "headline": "First Shipment to the United States",
      "text": "In 1794, Hennessy made its first shipment of cognac to the United States, marking the beginning of its international expansion.",
      "date": "1794"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Star System",
      "text": "In 1865, Maurice Hennessy, the great-grandson of the founder, introduced the star system to classify cognacs, which is still used today.",
      "date": "1865"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of V.S.O.P.",
      "text": "In 1817, Hennessy created the V.S.O.P. (Very Superior Old Pale) cognac at the request of the future King George IV of Great Britain.",
      "date": "1817"
