      "headline": "Early 20th Century Emergence",
      "text": "Conversion therapy practices began to emerge in the early 20th century, with various methods being used to attempt to change an individual's sexual orientation or gender identity.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1950s and 1960s: Aversion Therapy",
      "text": "During the 1950s and 1960s, aversion therapy became a common method used in conversion therapy, involving electric shocks and nausea-inducing drugs.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1973: APA Removes Homosexuality from DSM",
      "text": "In 1973, the American Psychiatric Association (APA) removed homosexuality from the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM), marking a significant shift in the understanding of sexual orientation.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1990: World Health Organization Declassification",
      "text": "In 1990, the World Health Organization declassified homosexuality as a mental disorder, further discrediting conversion therapy practices.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "2000s: Growing Scientific Consensus",
      "text": "By the 2000s, a scientific consensus had formed that conversion therapy is ineffective and harmful, with numerous studies highlighting the psychological damage it can cause.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "2012: California Bans Conversion Therapy for Minors",
      "text": "In 2012, California became the first state in the United States to ban conversion therapy for minors, setting a precedent for other jurisdictions.",
      "date": "2012"
    },
    {
      "headline": "2015: White House Condemns Conversion Therapy",
      "text": "In 2015, the White House under President Barack Obama publicly condemned conversion therapy, calling for an end to the practice.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "2020: Global Movement Against Conversion Therapy",
      "text": "By 2020, an increasing number of countries and regions around the world had enacted laws banning conversion therapy, reflecting a growing global movement against the practice.",
      "date": "2020"
    }
  ]
}

