      "headline": "Operation Searchlight Begins",
      "text": "On 1971-03-25, Operation Searchlight was launched by the Pakistan Armed Forces to suppress the Bengali population in East Pakistan. This marked the beginning of the Bangladesh genocide.",
      "date": "1971-03-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mass Killings and Atrocities",
      "text": "Throughout 1971, Pakistani soldiers and local pro-Pakistan militias engaged in mass killings and atrocities against the Bengali population, including the systematic rape of Bengali women. Estimates suggest between 300,000 and 3,000,000 Bengalis were killed and between 200,000 and 400,000 women were raped.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "International Reaction and Reports",
      "text": "During the genocide, reports of the atrocities reached the international community, leading to widespread condemnation. The Geneva-based International Commission of Jurists later concluded that Pakistan's campaign involved attempts to exterminate or forcibly remove a significant portion of the country's Hindu populace.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Bangladesh Liberation War",
      "text": "The Bangladesh Liberation War ended on 1971-12-16 with the victory of the Bangladeshi forces and the Indian military intervention, leading to the independence of Bangladesh.",
      "date": "1971-12-16"
    }
  ]
}

