    },
    {
      "headline": "Moved to Paris",
      "text": "Leibniz moved to Paris in 1672, where he met prominent intellectuals and furthered his studies in mathematics and physics.",
      "date": "1672"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Developed Calculus Independently",
      "text": "By 1675, Leibniz had developed the fundamental principles of calculus independently of Isaac Newton.",
      "date": "1675"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'Nova Methodus pro Maximis et Minimis'",
      "text": "In 1684, Leibniz published 'Nova Methodus pro Maximis et Minimis', his first publication on calculus.",
      "date": "1684"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointed as Librarian at the Herzog August Library",
      "text": "In 1690, Leibniz was appointed as the librarian at the Herzog August Library in Wolfenbüttel.",
      "date": "1690"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'Essais de Théodicée'",
      "text": "In 1710, Leibniz published 'Essais de Théodicée', a philosophical work addressing the problem of evil.",
