      "headline": "Foundation of Nottingham",
      "text": "Nottingham was originally a settlement established by the Anglo-Saxons. The name 'Nottingham' is derived from 'Snotingaham', meaning 'the homestead of Snot's people'.",
      "date": "-0600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Norman Conquest",
      "text": "Following the Norman Conquest of England in 1066, Nottingham became an important military stronghold.",
      "date": "1066"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of Nottingham Castle",
      "text": "Nottingham Castle was built in 1068 by William the Conqueror as a wooden motte-and-bailey structure.",
      "date": "1068"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Charter of Nottingham",
      "text": "In 1155, Nottingham was granted its first charter by King Henry II, allowing it to hold a market.",
      "date": "1155"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rebuilding of Nottingham Castle",
      "text": "In 1170, the wooden structure of Nottingham Castle was replaced with a stone castle.",
      "date": "1170"
    },
    {
