      "text": "The world's first high-speed rail service began in Japan with the inauguration of the Shinkansen, also known as the 'bullet train', on October 1, 1964. The initial line connected Tokyo and Osaka, covering the distance in about four hours.",
      "date": "1964-10-01"
    },
