      "text": "Apple introduced the Lisa computer in 1983, which was one of the first personal computers to use a mouse. The Macintosh, released in 1984, further popularized the mouse.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Optical Mouse",
      "text": "The first optical mouse, which used light to detect movement, was developed by Richard F. Lyon at Xerox in 1980, but it became commercially viable in the late 1990s.",
      "date": "1999"
