      "text": "Humayun faced another defeat at the hands of Sher Shah Suri at the Battle of Kannauj on May 17, 1540, leading to his loss of the Mughal Empire.",
      "date": "1540-05-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile in Persia",
      "text": "After losing his empire, Humayun sought refuge in Persia in 1540, where he was received by the Safavid ruler Shah Tahmasp I.",
      "date": "1540"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Power",
      "text": "With Persian support, Humayun regained control of Delhi on July 23, 1555, re-establishing the Mughal Empire.",
      "date": "1555-07-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Humayun",
      "text": "Humayun died on January 27, 1556, after falling down the stairs of his library in Delhi.",
      "date": "1556-01-27"
    }
  ]
}

