      "text": "The First Intifada, which began in December 1987, increased the demand for UNRWA's services in the occupied Palestinian territories.",
      "date": "1987-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Oslo Accords",
      "text": "The signing of the Oslo Accords in 1993 led to changes in the political landscape, affecting UNRWA's operations and its coordination with the newly established Palestinian Authority.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Intifada",
      "text": "The outbreak of the Second Intifada in September 2000 resulted in increased violence and a greater need for UNRWA's humanitarian assistance in the region.",
      "date": "2000-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Syria Conflict",
      "text": "The Syrian Civil War, beginning in 2011, severely impacted Palestinian refugees in Syria, leading to a humanitarian crisis that UNRWA has been addressing.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
