      "headline": "Richard Karp's Contribution",
      "text": "In 1972, Richard Karp published a paper titled 'Reducibility Among Combinatorial Problems', which further explored the P versus NP problem and identified 21 NP-complete problems, demonstrating their interrelation.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cook-Levin Theorem",
      "text": "The Cook-Levin theorem, proven by Stephen Cook and independently by Leonid Levin, establishes that the Boolean satisfiability problem is NP-complete. This theorem is a cornerstone in the study of computational complexity.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Clay Mathematics Institute Millennium Prize",
      "text": "In 2000, the Clay Mathematics Institute included the P versus NP problem as one of the seven Millennium Prize Problems, offering a $1 million prize for a correct solution.",
      "date": "2000"
    }
  ]
}

