      "text": "Grace Brewster Murray was born on December 9, 1906, in New York City, USA.",
      "date": "1906-12-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Graduation from Vassar College",
      "text": "In 1928, Grace Hopper graduated from Vassar College with a bachelor's degree in mathematics and physics.",
      "date": "1928"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ph.D. in Mathematics from Yale University",
      "text": "Grace Hopper earned her Ph.D. in mathematics from Yale University in 1934.",
      "date": "1934"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joined the U.S. Naval Reserve",
      "text": "In 1943, during World War II, Grace Hopper joined the U.S. Naval Reserve and was assigned to the Bureau of Ships Computation Project at Harvard University.",
      "date": "1943"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Worked on Harvard Mark I",
      "text": "Grace Hopper was one of the first programmers of the Harvard Mark I computer in 1944.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Published 'A Manual of Operation for the Automatic Sequence Controlled Calculator'",
      "text": "In 1946, Grace Hopper published 'A Manual of Operation for the Automatic Sequence Controlled Calculator', the first computer manual.",
      "date": "1946"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Developed the first compiler",
      "text": "In 1952, Grace Hopper developed the first compiler for a computer programming language, which was a significant milestone in computer science.",
      "date": "1952"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Developed FLOW-MATIC",
      "text": "In 1955, Grace Hopper developed FLOW-MATIC, the first English-like data processing language, which was a precursor to COBOL.",
      "date": "1955"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Contributed to the development of COBOL",
      "text": "In 1959, Grace Hopper was instrumental in the development of COBOL, one of the first high-level programming languages.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Promoted to Rear Admiral",
      "text": "In 1985, Grace Hopper was promoted to the rank of Rear Admiral in the United States Navy.",
      "date": "1985"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Retirement from the Navy",
      "text": "Grace Hopper retired from the United States Navy in 1986 at the age of 79.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Grace Hopper",
      "text": "Grace Hopper passed away on January 1, 1992, in Arlington, Virginia, USA.",
      "date": "1992-01-01"
    }
  ]
}

