      "text": "Vaishnavism traces its origins to the Vedic period, with references to Vishnu found in the Rigveda, which dates back to around 1500-1200 BCE.",
      "date": "-1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Vaishnavism",
      "text": "Vaishnavism began to develop as a distinct tradition within Hinduism during the early centuries of the Common Era, with the composition of texts such as the Bhagavad Gita and the Puranas.",
