      "text": "On December 5, 1994, the Budapest Memorandum on Security Assurances was signed at the OSCE conference in Budapest, Hungary. The memorandum provided security assurances by its signatories, which included Russia, the United States, and the United Kingdom, to Belarus, Kazakhstan, and Ukraine in relation to their accession to the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons (NPT).",
