    {
      "headline": "Constitution of 1933",
      "text": "The new Constitution of 1933 was adopted, which laid the foundation for the Estado Novo's corporatist and authoritarian structure.",
      "date": "1933"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II Neutrality",
      "text": "During World War II, Portugal, under Salazar's Estado Novo, maintained a position of neutrality, although it allowed the Allies to use the Azores as a base.",
