      "headline": "Death of Cleopatra",
      "text": "Cleopatra VII, the last ruler of Ptolemaic Egypt, died on either 10 or 12 August, 30 BC, in Alexandria. According to popular belief, Cleopatra killed herself by allowing an asp to bite her. However, Roman-era writers such as Strabo, Plutarch, and Cassius Dio suggest she poisoned herself using either a toxic ointment or a sharp implement like a hairpin. Modern scholars debate these accounts, with some suggesting she was forced to commit suicide by her Roman rival Octavian.",
