      "headline": "Armistice Day Becomes a Legal Holiday",
      "text": "In 1938, Armistice Day was made a legal holiday in the United States, dedicated to the cause of world peace and to honor World War I veterans.",
      "date": "1938"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming to Veterans Day",
      "text": "At the urging of major U.S. veteran organizations, Armistice Day was renamed Veterans Day in 1954 to honor American veterans of all wars.",
      "date": "1954"
    },
