      "headline": "Uniform Monday Holiday Act",
      "text": "In 1968, the Uniform Monday Holiday Act was signed, which moved Veterans Day to the fourth Monday in October. The law took effect in 1971.",
      "date": "1968"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Veterans Day Restored to November 11",
      "text": "In 1975, President Gerald Ford signed a law returning Veterans Day to November 11, due to the historical significance of the date. The change took effect in 1978.",
      "date": "1975"
    }
  ]
