      "text": "On October 3, 1967, William J. Knight flew the X-15 at a speed of 4,520 miles per hour (Mach 6.7) at an altitude of 102,100 feet (31,120 meters), setting the official world record for the highest speed ever recorded by a crewed, powered aircraft.",
