      "text": "Approximately 252 million years ago, the Permian-Triassic extinction event, also known as the 'Great Dying', occurred. It is the Earth's most severe extinction event, with an estimated 90-96% of marine species and 70% of terrestrial vertebrate species becoming extinct.",
      "date": "-0252000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Triassic-Jurassic Extinction Event",
      "text": "Around 201 million years ago, the Triassic-Jurassic extinction event occurred. It resulted in the extinction of about 76% of all marine and terrestrial species.",
      "date": "-0201000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cretaceous-Paleogene Extinction Event",
      "text": "Approximately 66 million years ago, the Cretaceous-Paleogene extinction event took place. It is famously known for the extinction of the non-avian dinosaurs, along with about 75% of all species on Earth.",
      "date": "-0066000000"
    }
  ]
}

