      "text": "On April 20, 1792, the French Legislative Assembly declared war on Austria, marking the beginning of the French Revolutionary Wars.",
      "date": "1792-04-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Valmy",
      "text": "On September 20, 1792, the French army achieved a significant victory against the Prussian forces at the Battle of Valmy, boosting French morale and solidifying the revolution.",
      "date": "1792-09-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Execution of King Louis XVI",
      "text": "On January 21, 1793, King Louis XVI of France was executed by guillotine, escalating tensions and solidifying the coalition against France.",
      "date": "1793-01-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Fleurus",
      "text": "On June 26, 1794, the French army won a decisive victory at the Battle of Fleurus, leading to the French occupation of Belgium.",
      "date": "1794-06-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Campo Formio",
      "text": "On October 17, 1797, the Treaty of Campo Formio was signed, ending the War of the First Coalition and resulting in territorial gains for France.",
      "date": "1797-10-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Second Coalition",
      "text": "In 1798, a new coalition formed against France, including Great Britain, Austria, Russia, and others, marking the beginning of the War of the Second Coalition.",
      "date": "1798"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of the Nile",
      "text": "On August 1-3, 1798, the British navy, led by Admiral Horatio Nelson, defeated the French fleet at the Battle of the Nile, securing British control of the Mediterranean.",
      "date": "1798-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Marengo",
      "text": "On June 14, 1800, Napoleon Bonaparte led French forces to victory against the Austrians at the Battle of Marengo, solidifying his power in France.",
      "date": "1800-06-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Lunéville",
      "text": "On February 9, 1801, the Treaty of Lunéville was signed between France and Austria, effectively ending the War of the Second Coalition.",
      "date": "1801-02-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Amiens",
      "text": "On March 25, 1802, the Treaty of Amiens was signed between France and Great Britain, temporarily ending hostilities and marking the end of the French Revolutionary Wars.",
      "date": "1802-03-25"
    }
  ]
}

