      "headline": "Charge of the Light Brigade",
      "text": "On 25 October 1854, during the Battle of Balaclava in the Crimean War, the British Light Brigade, led by Lord Cardigan, mounted a frontal assault against a well-prepared Russian artillery battery. The charge resulted from a misunderstood order from the commander-in-chief, Lord Raglan. The Light Brigade charged under heavy fire, reached the Russian positions, scattered some gunners, but was forced to retreat immediately, suffering heavy casualties.",
