      "headline": "Start of the Yalta Conference",
      "text": "The Yalta Conference began on February 4, 1945. It was a World War II meeting of the heads of government of the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Soviet Union to discuss the postwar reorganization of Germany and Europe.",
      "date": "1945-02-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Participants of the Conference",
      "text": "The conference was attended by President Franklin D. Roosevelt of the United States, Prime Minister Winston Churchill of the United Kingdom, and General Secretary Joseph Stalin of the Soviet Union.",
      "date": "1945-02-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Location of the Conference",
      "text": "The conference was held near Yalta in Crimea, Soviet Union, within the Livadia, Yusupov, and Vorontsov palaces.",
      "date": "1945-02-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Yalta Conference",
      "text": "The Yalta Conference concluded on February 11, 1945. The leaders reached several agreements on the reorganization of postwar Europe, including the division of Germany into occupation zones.",
      "date": "1945-02-11"
    }
  ]
}

