      "headline": "Abolishment of Income Tax",
      "text": "The income tax was repealed in 1872 after the Civil War ended.",
      "date": "1872"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reinstatement of Income Tax",
      "text": "The income tax was reinstated in 1894, but was later declared unconstitutional by the Supreme Court in 1895.",
      "date": "1894"
    },
    {
      "headline": "16th Amendment Ratified",
      "text": "The 16th Amendment to the U.S. Constitution was ratified in 1913, allowing Congress to levy an income tax without apportioning it among the states.",
      "date": "1913"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IRS Reorganization",
      "text": "In 1953, the Bureau of Internal Revenue was reorganized and renamed the Internal Revenue Service.",
      "date": "1953"
    },
