      "text": "Doggerland was formed during the Late Pleistocene and Early Holocene, as the region was exposed due to the lowering of sea levels during glacial periods.",
      "date": "-012000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Doggerland at its Largest",
      "text": "Around 10,000 years ago, Doggerland was at its largest, stretching across the region between what is now the east coast of Great Britain, the Netherlands, the western coast of Germany, and the Danish peninsula of Jutland.",
      "date": "-08000"
