    {
      "headline": "Formation of Scandinavian Airlines System",
      "text": "Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) was founded on August 1, 1946, as a consortium to pool the transatlantic operations of three Scandinavian airlines: Det Danske Luftfartselskab (DDL) of Denmark, Svensk Interkontinental Lufttrafik AB (SILA) of Sweden, and Det Norske Luftfartselskap (DNL) of Norway.",
      "date": "1946-08-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Transatlantic Flight",
      "text": "On September 17, 1946, SAS operated its first transatlantic flight from Stockholm to New York City, marking the beginning of its international operations.",
