      "headline": "Treaty of Tordesillas",
      "text": "On June 7, 1494, Ferdinand and Isabella signed the Treaty of Tordesillas with Portugal, dividing the newly discovered lands outside Europe.",
      "date": "1494-06-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Isabella I of Castile",
      "text": "Isabella I of Castile died on November 26, 1504, leaving Ferdinand as the regent of Castile for their daughter, Joanna.",
      "date": "1504-11-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Regency of Castile",
      "text": "After Isabella's death in 1504, Ferdinand served as the regent of Castile until 1506, when Joanna's husband, Philip the Handsome, took over.",
      "date": "1504"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Germaine of Foix",
      "text": "Ferdinand married Germaine of Foix on October 19, 1505, in an attempt to produce a male heir for the Crown of Aragon.",
      "date": "1505-10-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ferdinand II of Aragon",
      "text": "Ferdinand II of Aragon died on January 23, 1516, in Madrigalejo, Extremadura, Spain.",
