      "headline": "Founding of the People's Republic of China",
      "text": "On October 1, 1949, Zhou Enlai became the inaugural Premier of the People's Republic of China and concurrently served as the Minister of Foreign Affairs.",
      "date": "1949-10-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Geneva Conference",
      "text": "In 1954, Zhou Enlai played a crucial role in the Geneva Conference, which addressed issues related to the Korean War and the First Indochina War.",
      "date": "1954"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bandung Conference",
      "text": "In April 1955, Zhou Enlai attended the Bandung Conference, which was a meeting of Asian and African states, most of which were newly independent.",
      "date": "1955-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cultural Revolution",
      "text": "During the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976), Zhou Enlai worked to moderate some of the excesses and maintain government functions.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
