      "headline": "Anne Frank's Last Diary Entry",
      "text": "Anne Frank made her last diary entry on August 1, 1944. She continued to write in her diary throughout her time in hiding.",
      "date": "1944-08-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrest of the Frank Family",
      "text": "On August 4, 1944, the Frank family and the others hiding with them were discovered and arrested by the Gestapo.",
      "date": "1944-08-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Anne Frank Dies in Bergen-Belsen",
      "text": "In February or March 1945, Anne Frank died of typhus in the Bergen-Belsen concentration camp, just weeks before the camp was liberated.",
      "date": "1945-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Otto Frank Receives Anne's Diaries",
      "text": "After the war ended in 1945, Miep Gies and Bep Voskuijl, who had helped the Frank family while they were in hiding, gave Anne's diaries to Otto Frank, the only surviving member of the family.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of The Diary of a Young Girl",
      "text": "In 1947, Otto Frank arranged for the publication of Anne's diary, which was first published in Dutch as 'Het Achterhuis' (The Secret Annex).",
      "date": "1947"
    }
  ]
}

