      "headline": "Biblical Mention of the Holy Lance",
      "text": "The Holy Lance is mentioned in the Christian Bible as the lance that pierced the side of Jesus during his crucifixion. This event is traditionally dated to around 30-33 AD.",
      "date": "0030"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appearance of Relics in Jerusalem",
      "text": "Relics purported to be the Holy Lance began to appear as early as the 6th century, originally in Jerusalem.",
      "date": "0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Holy Lance in Constantinople",
      "text": "By the 7th century, a relic believed to be the Holy Lance was moved to Constantinople, where it was kept in the church of Hagia Sophia.",
      "date": "0600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Holy Lance in Antioch",
      "text": "During the First Crusade, in 1098, a relic claimed to be the Holy Lance was discovered in Antioch by a monk named Peter Bartholomew.",
      "date": "1098"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Holy Lance in Vienna",
      "text": "By the 13th century, a relic identified as the Holy Lance was in the possession of the Holy Roman Emperors and was kept in Vienna.",
      "date": "1200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Holy Lance in Nuremberg",
      "text": "In 1424, the Holy Roman Emperor Sigismund transferred the Holy Lance to Nuremberg, where it was kept as part of the Imperial Regalia.",
      "date": "1424"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Holy Lance in Vienna (Return)",
      "text": "After the Napoleonic Wars, the Holy Lance was returned to Vienna, where it remains today in the Hofburg Palace.",
