      "headline": "Reign of King Wu Ding",
      "text": "King Wu Ding is one of the most notable rulers of the Shang dynasty, known for his military campaigns and expansion of the dynasty's influence. His reign is dated to the late 13th century BC.",
      "date": "-1250"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capital at Yin",
      "text": "The Shang dynasty moved its capital to Yin, near modern-day Anyang, around 1300 BC. This site has provided significant archaeological evidence of the Shang dynasty's existence.",
      "date": "-1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Shang Dynasty",
      "text": "The Shang dynasty came to an end around 1046 BC when it was overthrown by the Zhou dynasty. The last Shang king, King Zhou, was defeated at the Battle of Muye.",
      "date": "-1046"
    }
  ]
}

