      "text": "Following the skirmish at Lexington, British troops moved on to Concord. At the North Bridge in Concord, approximately 400 militiamen engaged the British forces, forcing them to retreat.",
      "date": "1775-04-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Retreat to Boston",
      "text": "After the confrontation at Concord, British forces began their retreat to Boston. Along the way, they were continually harassed by militia forces, suffering significant casualties.",
      "date": "1775-04-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Militia Support and Siege of Boston",
      "text": "The battles resulted in an outpouring of militia support for the anti-British cause. Thousands of militiamen from surrounding colonies gathered and began the Siege of Boston, effectively trapping the British forces in the city.",
      "date": "1775-04"
    }
  ]
}

{
