      "text": "The Cyberathlete Professional League (CPL) was founded in 1997 by Angel Munoz. It was one of the first major esports organizations and helped popularize competitive gaming.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Launch of Major League Gaming (MLG)",
      "text": "Major League Gaming (MLG) was founded in 2002 by Sundance DiGiovanni and Mike Sepso. MLG became one of the largest esports organizations in North America.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The First Dota 2 International Tournament",
      "text": "In 2011, Valve Corporation hosted the first Dota 2 International tournament, which featured a prize pool of $1.6 million, setting a new standard for esports prize money.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "League of Legends World Championship",
      "text": "The first League of Legends World Championship was held in 2011 at DreamHack in Sweden. It marked the beginning of one of the most popular annual esports events.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Esports Recognized by the International Olympic Committee",
      "text": "In 2017, the International Olympic Committee recognized esports as a sporting activity, opening the door for potential inclusion in future Olympic Games.",
      "date": "2017"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Esports at the Asian Games",
      "text": "Esports was included as a demonstration sport at the 2018 Asian Games in Jakarta, Indonesia, marking a significant milestone in the recognition of esports as a legitimate competitive activity.",
