      "text": "On June 20, 1863, West Virginia was admitted to the Union after separating from Virginia, which had seceded.",
      "date": "1863-06-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Civil War",
      "text": "On April 9, 1865, Confederate General Robert E. Lee surrendered to Union General Ulysses S. Grant at Appomattox Court House, effectively ending the Civil War.",
      "date": "1865-04-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reconstruction and Readmission",
      "text": "From 1866 to 1870, the seceded states were gradually readmitted to the Union during the Reconstruction era.",
      "date": "1866"
    }
  ]
}

