      "text": "The earliest evidence of tattooing dates back to the Neolithic period, with tattoos found on mummified skin. The oldest known tattoos were found on the body of Ötzi the Iceman, dating back to around 3300 BCE.",
      "date": "-3300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tattooing in Ancient Egypt",
      "text": "Tattooing was practiced in ancient Egypt, as evidenced by tattoos found on female mummies dating back to around 2000 BCE. These tattoos were often associated with fertility and rejuvenation.",
      "date": "-2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tattooing in Ancient China",
      "text": "In ancient China, tattoos were used as a form of punishment and were considered a mark of shame. This practice dates back to around 500 BCE.",
      "date": "-0500"
