    },
    {
      "headline": "Tattooing in the 20th Century",
      "text": "Throughout the 20th century, tattoos became increasingly popular in Western cultures, evolving from a subculture to mainstream acceptance. This period saw the rise of tattoo parlors and the professionalization of tattoo artists.",
      "date": "1900"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Tattoo Culture",
      "text": "In the 21st century, tattoos have become a widely accepted form of self-expression and art, with diverse styles and techniques being celebrated globally. The cultural significance of tattoos continues to evolve.",
      "date": "2000"
    }
