      "headline": "Construction of the Great Pyramid of Giza",
      "text": "The Great Pyramid of Giza, also known as the Pyramid of Khufu, was constructed during the reign of Pharaoh Khufu around 2580–2560 BCE. It is the largest of the three pyramids in the Giza pyramid complex.",
      "date": "-2580"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Pyramid of Khafre",
      "text": "The Pyramid of Khafre, the second largest pyramid in the Giza pyramid complex, was built during the reign of Pharaoh Khafre around 2570 BCE. It is known for its preserved casing stones at the top.",
      "date": "-2570"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Great Sphinx",
      "text": "The Great Sphinx, a limestone statue with the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh, is believed to have been constructed during the reign of Pharaoh Khafre around 2570 BCE, near his pyramid.",
      "date": "-2570"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Pyramid of Menkaure",
      "text": "The Pyramid of Menkaure, the smallest of the three main pyramids at Giza, was constructed during the reign of Pharaoh Menkaure around 2510 BCE.",
      "date": "-2510"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Associated Pyramid Complexes",
      "text": "Each of the three main pyramids at Giza was part of a larger complex that included temples, smaller pyramids, and other structures, developed during the Fourth Dynasty of the Old Kingdom.",
      "date": "-2500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Cemeteries and Workers' Village",
      "text": "The Giza pyramid complex also includes several cemeteries and the remains of a workers' village, which were established to support the construction and maintenance of the pyramids.",
      "date": "-2500"
    }
  ]
}

