      "headline": "Birth of Juliane Koepcke",
      "text": "Juliane Margaret Beate Koepcke was born on October 10, 1954, in Lima, Peru, to German zoologists Maria and Hans-Wilhelm Koepcke.",
      "date": "1954-10-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "LANSA Flight 508 Crash",
      "text": "On December 24, 1971, Juliane Koepcke was the sole survivor of the LANSA Flight 508 plane crash. The plane was struck by lightning and broke up in mid-air, causing her to fall 3,000 meters (10,000 feet) while strapped to her seat.",
      "date": "1971-12-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Survival in the Amazon Rainforest",
      "text": "After the crash, Juliane Koepcke survived for 11 days alone in the Peruvian Amazon rainforest. Despite suffering numerous injuries, she managed to find a stream and followed it until she was rescued by local lumberjacks on January 3, 1972.",
      "date": "1972-01-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'When I Fell From the Sky'",
      "text": "In 2011, Juliane Koepcke published her memoir 'When I Fell From the Sky', detailing her experience as the sole survivor of the LANSA Flight 508 crash and her subsequent survival in the rainforest.",
      "date": "2011"
    }
  ]
}

