    {
      "headline": "Origin of the Term 'Folk Music'",
      "text": "The term 'folk music' originated in the 19th century. It was used to describe music that was transmitted orally, had unknown composers, and was played on traditional instruments.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Folk Music in the 19th Century",
      "text": "During the 19th century, folk music was recognized as a distinct genre, often associated with cultural or national identity and performed by custom over a long period of time.",
