      "headline": "Rudolf Diesel Patents Diesel Engine",
      "text": "Rudolf Diesel was granted a patent for his design of the diesel engine on February 23, 1893. This marked the beginning of the development of the diesel engine, which operates on the principle of compression ignition.",
      "date": "1893-02-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Diesel Engine Prototype",
      "text": "In 1897, Rudolf Diesel built the first successful prototype of the diesel engine at the Augsburg machine works. This engine was more efficient than the steam engines of the time.",
      "date": "1897"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Commercial Diesel Engine",
      "text": "The first commercial diesel engine was produced in 1898. It was used for stationary applications such as pumping and electricity generation.",
      "date": "1898"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Diesel Engine in Marine Use",
      "text": "In 1903, the French submarine Aigrette became the first submarine to be powered by a diesel engine, demonstrating the engine's potential for marine applications.",
      "date": "1903"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Diesel Engine in Rail Transport",
      "text": "The first diesel-powered locomotive was introduced in 1912 by the Swiss company Sulzer. This marked the beginning of diesel engines in rail transport.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Diesel Engine in Road Vehicles",
      "text": "In 1923, the first diesel-powered trucks were produced by MAN and Benz. This development extended the use of diesel engines to road vehicles.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Turbocharging in Diesel Engines",
      "text": "In 1951, turbocharging was introduced to diesel engines, significantly improving their power output and efficiency.",
      "date": "1951"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Common Rail Diesel Technology",
      "text": "In the late 1990s, common rail diesel technology was introduced, allowing for more precise control of fuel injection and improving engine performance and emissions.",
      "date": "1990s"
    }
  ]
}

