      "headline": "Assassination of Orlando Letelier",
      "text": "On September 21, 1976, Orlando Letelier, a former Chilean ambassador and critic of Pinochet, was assassinated in Washington, D.C., in a car bomb attack orchestrated by Operation Condor.",
      "date": "1976-09-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Human Rights Violations",
      "text": "During its operation, Condor was responsible for numerous human rights violations, including the disappearance and murder of thousands of political dissidents across South America.",
      "date": "1977"
