      "headline": "Continued Use and Secret Recipe",
      "text": "Throughout the 8th to 12th centuries, Greek fire continued to be a closely-guarded state secret of the Byzantine Empire. Its exact composition remains unknown, but it was likely based on petroleum mixed with resins.",
      "date": "0800"
