      "headline": "Invention of the Barcode",
      "text": "In 1948, Bernard Silver and Norman Joseph Woodland began working on a system to automatically read product information during checkout at a grocery store. This led to the development of the barcode.",
      "date": "1948"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Patent Filed for Barcode Technology",
      "text": "On October 20, 1949, Norman Joseph Woodland and Bernard Silver filed a patent application for their barcode technology.",
      "date": "1949-10-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Patent Granted for Barcode",
      "text": "On October 7, 1952, the patent for the barcode was granted to Norman Joseph Woodland and Bernard Silver.",
      "date": "1952-10-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Universal Product Code (UPC)",
      "text": "In 1973, the Universal Product Code (UPC) was introduced, which standardized the barcode system for retail products.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First UPC Barcode Scanned",
      "text": "On June 26, 1974, the first UPC barcode was scanned at a Marsh's supermarket in Troy, Ohio. The product was a pack of Wrigley's Juicy Fruit gum.",
      "date": "1974-06-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of the QR Code",
      "text": "In 1994, the QR code, a type of two-dimensional barcode, was developed by Denso Wave, a subsidiary of Toyota, to track vehicles during manufacturing.",
      "date": "1994"
    }
  ]
}

