      "headline": "Civil Rights Act and Voting Rights Act",
      "text": "The Confederate flag was prominently displayed in opposition to the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and the Voting Rights Act of 1965, symbolizing resistance to desegregation and civil rights for African Americans.",
      "date": "1964"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Charleston Church Shooting",
      "text": "In 2015, the Confederate flag became a focal point of national debate following the Charleston church shooting, where nine African Americans were killed by a white supremacist who had posed with the flag.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
