      "text": "In 1565, Ivan IV established the Oprichnina, a policy that divided the Russian state and led to a period of political terror.",
      "date": "1565"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Livonian War",
      "text": "The Livonian War ended in 1583 with the Treaty of Plussa, resulting in Russia losing access to the Baltic Sea.",
      "date": "1583"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Time of Troubles Begins",
      "text": "In 1598, the Time of Troubles began following the death of Tsar Feodor I, leading to a period of political instability and famine.",
      "date": "1598"
    },
    {
      "headline": "False Dmitry I Seizes Power",
      "text": "In 1605, False Dmitry I, a pretender to the Russian throne, seized power in Moscow, marking a significant event during the Time of Troubles.",
      "date": "1605"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Romanov Dynasty Begins",
      "text": "In 1613, Michael Romanov was elected Tsar, marking the end of the Time of Troubles and the beginning of the Romanov dynasty.",
      "date": "1613"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russo-Polish War Ends",
      "text": "In 1667, the Russo-Polish War ended with the Treaty of Andrusovo, resulting in Russia gaining control of Left-bank Ukraine and Kiev.",
      "date": "1667"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Streltsy Uprising",
      "text": "In 1682, the Streltsy Uprising occurred, a revolt by the Russian military corps known as the Streltsy, which was suppressed by the government.",
      "date": "1682"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peter the Great Becomes Sole Ruler",
      "text": "In 1696, Peter the Great became the sole ruler of Russia after the death of his half-brother Ivan V.",
      "date": "1696"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Great Northern War Begins",
      "text": "In 1700, the Great Northern War began as Russia, under Peter the Great, sought to challenge Swedish dominance in the Baltic region.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Foundation of Saint Petersburg",
      "text": "In 1703, Peter the Great founded the city of Saint Petersburg, which would later become the capital of Russia.",
      "date": "1703"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Poltava",
      "text": "In 1709, the Battle of Poltava took place, where Russian forces decisively defeated the Swedish army, marking a turning point in the Great Northern War.",
      "date": "1709"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Great Northern War",
      "text": "In 1721, the Great Northern War ended with the Treaty of Nystad, establishing Russia as a major European power and marking the foundation of the Russian Empire.",
      "date": "1721"
    }
  ]
}

