      "headline": "Significance in Cooking",
      "text": "The Maillard reaction is crucial in cooking, as it occurs in a variety of foods such as seared steaks, fried dumplings, cookies, breads, and toasted marshmallows, contributing to their distinctive flavors and aromas.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Temperature Range for Reaction",
      "text": "The Maillard reaction typically proceeds rapidly from around 140 to 165 °C, making it an important consideration in recipes that require browning.",
