      "headline": "First Settlement",
      "text": "The first known settlement in the Skopje area dates back to at least 4000 BCE, when the Neolithic people established a settlement here.",
      "date": "-4000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Era",
      "text": "In 164 BCE, the Romans conquered the area and established the city of Scupi, which became an important regional center.",
      "date": "-0164"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction by Earthquake",
      "text": "In 518, Scupi was destroyed by a massive earthquake, leading to significant changes in the city's structure and population.",
      "date": "0518"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Byzantine Rule",
      "text": "Following the earthquake, the city was rebuilt and came under Byzantine rule, becoming an important military and administrative center.",
      "date": "0520"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bulgarian Empire Control",
      "text": "In the late 9th century, Skopje came under the control of the First Bulgarian Empire.",
      "date": "0890"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Conquest",
      "text": "In 1392, Skopje was conquered by the Ottoman Empire, marking the beginning of over 500 years of Ottoman rule.",
      "date": "1392"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Skopje as a Trade Center",
      "text": "During the Ottoman period, Skopje became an important trade center, with a diverse population and vibrant markets.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Great Fire of Skopje",
      "text": "In 1689, a great fire destroyed much of Skopje during the Great Turkish War.",
      "date": "1689"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Incorporation into Yugoslavia",
      "text": "After World War I, in 1918, Skopje became part of the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats, and Slovenes, later known as Yugoslavia.",
      "date": "1918"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Skopje Earthquake",
      "text": "On July 26, 1963, a devastating earthquake struck Skopje, killing over 1,000 people and leaving more than 200,000 homeless.",
      "date": "1963-07-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence of Macedonia",
      "text": "In 1991, following the breakup of Yugoslavia, Skopje became the capital of the newly independent Republic of Macedonia.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Skopje 2014 Project",
      "text": "In the 2010s, the Skopje 2014 project was launched, aiming to give the city a more classical appearance with new buildings and monuments.",
      "date": "2010"
