      "headline": "Popularity in the Song Dynasty",
      "text": "The Mid-Autumn Festival gained popularity during the Song Dynasty (960–1279 CE), becoming an important cultural event with moon worship and family gatherings.",
      "date": "0960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mooncakes as a Tradition",
      "text": "The tradition of eating mooncakes during the Mid-Autumn Festival became widespread during the Yuan Dynasty (1271–1368 CE).",
      "date": "1271"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zhu Yuanzhang's Rebellion",
      "text": "Legend has it that mooncakes were used to pass secret messages during Zhu Yuanzhang's rebellion against the Mongols, leading to the establishment of the Ming Dynasty in 1368.",
      "date": "1368"
    },
