      "text": "In 1935, the term 'Pneumonoultramicroscopicsilicovolcanoconiosis' was coined by Everett M. Smith, the then-president of the National Puzzlers' League. It was created as a deliberately long word to describe a lung disease caused by inhaling very fine ash and sand dust.",
