      "text": "Emiliano Zapata was born on August 8, 1879, in Anenecuilco, Morelos, Mexico.",
      "date": "1879-08-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zapata's Early Involvement in Land Rights",
      "text": "In 1909, Zapata was elected as the president of the board of defense for the village of Anenecuilco, where he began his involvement in defending land rights for peasants.",
      "date": "1909"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Plan of Ayala",
      "text": "On November 28, 1911, Zapata issued the Plan of Ayala, which called for land reforms and the redistribution of land to peasants.",
      "date": "1911-11-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zapata's Role in the Mexican Revolution",
      "text": "Zapata became a leading figure in the Mexican Revolution, which began in 1910, advocating for agrarian reform and the rights of peasants.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alliance with Pancho Villa",
      "text": "In 1914, Zapata formed an alliance with Pancho Villa, another revolutionary leader, to oppose the government of Venustiano Carranza.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zapata's Assassination",
      "text": "Emiliano Zapata was assassinated on April 10, 1919, in Chinameca, Morelos, Mexico, by forces loyal to Venustiano Carranza.",
      "date": "1919-04-10"
    }
  ]
}

