      "headline": "Formation of McDonald's Corporation",
      "text": "Ray Kroc founded the McDonald's Corporation in 1955 to facilitate the expansion of the franchise model.",
      "date": "1955"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Purchase of McDonald's Brand",
      "text": "In 1961, Ray Kroc bought the exclusive rights to the McDonald's name and operating system from the McDonald brothers for $2.7 million.",
      "date": "1961"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Filet-O-Fish",
      "text": "In 1962, McDonald's introduced the Filet-O-Fish sandwich, the first non-hamburger menu item, to cater to Catholic customers abstaining from meat on Fridays.",
      "date": "1962"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of the Big Mac",
      "text": "In 1967, McDonald's introduced the Big Mac, which became one of the company's most popular menu items.",
      "date": "1967"
