      "headline": "Formation of the Church of the East",
      "text": "The Church of the East was formed as a distinct Christian community in the Sasanian Empire, with its roots tracing back to the early Christian communities established in Mesopotamia. It became distinct from other Christian communities due to geographical and political factors.",
      "date": "0040"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Council of Seleucia-Ctesiphon",
      "text": "In 410, the Church of the East held the Council of Seleucia-Ctesiphon, which organized the church's structure and affirmed its independence from the Roman Empire's church.",
