      "headline": "Aftermath of the Battle",
      "text": "Although Harold Godwinson repelled the Norwegian invaders at the Battle of Stamford Bridge, his army was defeated by the Normans at the Battle of Hastings less than three weeks later, on 14 October 1066.",
      "date": "1066-10-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Viking Age",
      "text": "The Battle of Stamford Bridge has traditionally been presented as symbolising the end of the Viking Age. However, major Scandinavian campaigns in Britain and Ireland occurred in the following decades, such as those of King Sweyn Estrithson of Denmark in 1069–1070 and King Magnus Barefoot of Norway in 1098 and 1102–1103.",
      "date": "1066"
    }
  ]
}

