      "headline": "Beginning of Indian WhatsApp Lynchings",
      "text": "The spate of mob-related violence and killings in India, known as the Indian WhatsApp lynchings, began in May 2017. The violence was fueled by the spread of rumors, primarily relating to child-abduction and organ harvesting, via the WhatsApp message service.",
      "date": "2017-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jharkhand Lynchings",
      "text": "In May 2017, the first major incident occurred when seven men were killed in Jharkhand. This marked the beginning of the series of lynchings across India.",
      "date": "2017-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "National Attention",
      "text": "The lynchings did not become a matter of national attention until the beginning of 2018, when the frequency and severity of the incidents increased.",
      "date": "2018"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spread of Fake Messages",
      "text": "Fake messages, often customized with locally specific details, were circulated widely. These messages sometimes included real videos attached to fake claims, exacerbating the violence.",
      "date": "2018"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Government and Public Response",
      "text": "As the lynchings continued, there was increased public outcry and governmental pressure to address the spread of misinformation on WhatsApp and other social media platforms.",
      "date": "2018"
    }
  ]
}

