      "headline": "Murder of Kitty Genovese",
      "text": "In the early hours of March 13, 1964, Kitty Genovese was raped and stabbed outside the apartment building where she lived in the Kew Gardens neighborhood of Queens, New York.",
      "date": "1964-03-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The New York Times Article",
      "text": "On March 27, 1964, The New York Times published an article claiming that thirty-eight witnesses saw or heard the attack on Kitty Genovese, and that none of them called the police or came to her aid.",
      "date": "1964-03-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Bystander Effect",
      "text": "The murder of Kitty Genovese prompted inquiries into what became known as the bystander effect, or 'Genovese syndrome'. This psychological phenomenon became a staple of U.S. psychology textbooks for the next four decades.",
      "date": "1964"
    }
  ]
}

