      "headline": "Golden Bull of 1222",
      "text": "In 1222, King Andrew II of Hungary issued the Golden Bull, a significant constitutional document that limited the power of the monarchy and granted rights to the nobility.",
      "date": "1222"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Mohács",
      "text": "On August 29, 1526, the Hungarian forces were defeated by the Ottoman Empire at the Battle of Mohács, leading to the partition of Hungary.",
      "date": "1526-08-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Habsburg Rule",
      "text": "Following the Battle of Mohács and subsequent conflicts, Hungary came under Habsburg rule in the early 18th century, becoming part of the Habsburg Monarchy.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hungarian Revolution of 1848",
      "text": "In 1848, Hungarians revolted against Habsburg rule, seeking independence and democratic reforms. The revolution was ultimately suppressed in 1849.",
      "date": "1848"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Austro-Hungarian Compromise of 1867",
      "text": "In 1867, the Austro-Hungarian Compromise established the dual monarchy of Austria-Hungary, granting Hungary significant autonomy.",
      "date": "1867"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Trianon",
      "text": "On June 4, 1920, the Treaty of Trianon was signed, significantly reducing Hungary's territory and population following World War I.",
      "date": "1920-06-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hungarian Revolution of 1956",
      "text": "In 1956, a nationwide revolt against Soviet-imposed policies erupted in Hungary, which was eventually crushed by Soviet forces.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Communist Rule",
      "text": "In 1989, Hungary transitioned from a communist state to a democratic republic, marking the end of Soviet influence.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hungary Joins the European Union",
      "text": "On May 1, 2004, Hungary became a member of the European Union, integrating further into European political and economic structures.",
