      "text": "Santo Domingo was founded by Bartholomew Columbus, brother of Christopher Columbus, on the east bank of the Ozama River in 1496.",
      "date": "1496"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Relocation of Santo Domingo",
      "text": "In 1502, the city was relocated to the west bank of the Ozama River by Nicolás de Ovando after a hurricane destroyed the original settlement.",
      "date": "1502"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Cathedral in the Americas",
      "text": "The construction of the Cathedral of Santa María la Menor, the first cathedral in the Americas, began in 1512 and was completed in 1540.",
      "date": "1512"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Santo Domingo becomes the first seat of Spanish colonial rule",
      "text": "In 1511, Santo Domingo became the first seat of Spanish colonial rule in the New World.",
      "date": "1511"
