      "headline": "Founding of the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation",
      "text": "The Organisation of Islamic Cooperation (OIC) was founded on September 25, 1969, in response to an arson attack on the Al-Aqsa Mosque in Jerusalem. The organization was established to promote solidarity among Muslim countries and to safeguard their interests.",
      "date": "1969-09-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Islamic Summit Conference",
      "text": "The first Islamic Summit Conference was held in Rabat, Morocco, from September 22 to 25, 1969. This conference marked the formal establishment of the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation.",
      "date": "1969-09-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the OIC Charter",
      "text": "In March 1972, the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation adopted its charter, which laid down the objectives and principles of the organization, including the promotion of Islamic solidarity and cooperation among member states.",
      "date": "1972-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming to Organisation of Islamic Cooperation",
      "text": "In June 2011, the Organisation of the Islamic Conference was renamed the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation to better reflect its mission and objectives.",
      "date": "2011-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Islamic Development Bank",
      "text": "The Islamic Development Bank was established in 1975 as a specialized institution of the OIC to foster economic development and social progress in member countries.",
      "date": "1975"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Extraordinary Islamic Summit Conference",
      "text": "The first Extraordinary Islamic Summit Conference was held in Islamabad, Pakistan, in March 1997, focusing on the challenges faced by the Muslim world and the need for unity and cooperation.",
      "date": "1997-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Ten-Year Programme of Action",
      "text": "In December 2005, the OIC adopted a Ten-Year Programme of Action during the Third Extraordinary Session of the Islamic Summit Conference in Mecca, Saudi Arabia, to address issues such as poverty, education, and health in the Muslim world.",
      "date": "2005-12"
    }
  ]
}

