      "headline": "Birth of Jason",
      "text": "Jason was born as the son of Aeson, the rightful king of Iolcos. The exact date of his birth is not specified in Greek mythology.",
      "date": "-1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jason's Education by Chiron",
      "text": "Jason was sent to be educated by the centaur Chiron, who was known for his wisdom and knowledge. This event is part of his early life, but the exact date is not specified.",
      "date": "-1280"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jason's Return to Iolcos",
      "text": "Jason returned to Iolcos to claim his rightful throne from his uncle Pelias, who had usurped it from Jason's father, Aeson. This event marks the beginning of his quest for the Golden Fleece.",
      "date": "-1260"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Quest for the Golden Fleece",
      "text": "Jason embarked on the quest for the Golden Fleece, leading the Argonauts on a journey to Colchis. This is one of the most famous adventures in Greek mythology.",
      "date": "-1250"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jason's Marriage to Medea",
      "text": "During his quest for the Golden Fleece, Jason married Medea, the sorceress and granddaughter of the sun god Helios. This alliance was crucial for his success in obtaining the fleece.",
      "date": "-1245"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Iolcos with the Golden Fleece",
      "text": "Jason successfully returned to Iolcos with the Golden Fleece, aided by Medea's magic and cunning.",
      "date": "-1240"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Exile from Iolcos",
      "text": "Jason and Medea were exiled from Iolcos after Medea's revenge against Pelias, which involved the murder of Pelias by his own daughters, tricked by Medea.",
      "date": "-1235"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Settlement in Corinth",
      "text": "Jason and Medea settled in Corinth, where they lived for several years and had children.",
      "date": "-1230"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jason's Betrayal of Medea",
      "text": "Jason betrayed Medea by marrying Glauce, the daughter of the king of Corinth, leading to Medea's infamous revenge.",
      "date": "-1225"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Jason",
