      "headline": "Debate Among Medieval Theologians",
      "text": "During the medieval period, theologians debated the concept of the Immaculate Conception, discussing whether the Virgin Mary was free from original sin from the moment of her conception.",
      "date": "1100"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Council of Trent Affirms Mary's Freedom from Personal Sin",
      "text": "Between 1545 and 1563, the Council of Trent affirmed that the Virgin Mary was free from personal sin, although it did not define the Immaculate Conception as a dogma.",
      "date": "1545"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Definition of the Immaculate Conception as Dogma",
      "text": "On December 8, 1854, Pope Pius IX defined the Immaculate Conception as a dogma of the Catholic Church in the papal bull Ineffabilis Deus, stating that the Virgin Mary was free of original sin from the moment of her conception.",
      "date": "1854-12-08"
    }
  ]
}

