    {
      "headline": "Origins of Tango",
      "text": "The tango originated in the 1880s along the Río de la Plata, the natural border between Argentina and Uruguay. It was born in the impoverished port areas of these countries from a combination of Argentine Milonga, Spanish-Cuban Habanera, and Uruguayan Candombe celebrations.",
      "date": "1880"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tango in Brothels and Bars",
      "text": "During the late 19th century, tango was frequently practiced in the brothels and bars of ports, where business owners employed bands to entertain their patrons.",
