      "headline": "Approval for Opioid Use Disorder",
      "text": "Methadone was approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for the treatment of opioid use disorder in the 1970s. It became a key component of medication-assisted treatment (MAT) programs.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Methadone Maintenance Treatment",
      "text": "Methadone maintenance treatment (MMT) became widely recognized as an effective treatment for opioid addiction. It helps reduce cravings and withdrawal symptoms, allowing individuals to stabilize their lives.",
      "date": "1970s"
    },
