      "text": "The second moonwalk took place on December 12, 1972, during which Cernan and Schmitt collected lunar samples and deployed scientific instruments.",
      "date": "1972-12-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Third Moonwalk",
      "text": "The third and final moonwalk occurred on December 13, 1972, where the astronauts continued their scientific exploration and sample collection.",
      "date": "1972-12-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lunar Module Ascent",
      "text": "On December 14, 1972, the Lunar Module Challenger ascended from the Moon's surface, rejoining the Command Module in lunar orbit.",
      "date": "1972-12-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Earth",
      "text": "Apollo 17 returned to Earth on December 19, 1972, with a splashdown in the Pacific Ocean, marking the end of the Apollo lunar missions.",
      "date": "1972-12-19"
