      "headline": "First Introduction of the Ruble",
      "text": "The ruble was first introduced as a currency in Russia in the 14th century. It was initially a unit of weight for silver and later became a monetary unit.",
      "date": "1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decimalization of the Ruble",
      "text": "In 1704, under the reign of Peter the Great, the ruble became the first currency in the world to be decimalized, divided into 100 kopecks.",
      "date": "1704"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Paper Rubles",
      "text": "Paper rubles were introduced in Russia in 1769, marking a significant development in the currency's history.",
      "date": "1769"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Soviet Ruble Introduction",
      "text": "Following the Russian Revolution, the Soviet ruble was introduced in 1917 as the currency of the Soviet Union.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reform and Devaluation",
      "text": "In 1922-1923, a monetary reform was carried out in the Soviet Union, which included the devaluation of the ruble and the introduction of the chervonets.",
      "date": "1922"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-Soviet Ruble",
      "text": "After the dissolution of the Soviet Union in 1991, the Russian ruble replaced the Soviet ruble as the currency of the Russian Federation.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1998 Russian Financial Crisis",
      "text": "In August 1998, Russia experienced a financial crisis that led to the devaluation of the ruble and a default on domestic debt.",
      "date": "1998-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the New Ruble",
      "text": "In 1998, a new ruble was introduced, with 1 new ruble equaling 1,000 old rubles, as part of a redenomination process.",
      "date": "1998"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crimean Annexation and Sanctions",
      "text": "Following the annexation of Crimea in 2014, the ruble faced significant devaluation due to international sanctions and falling oil prices.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ruble in Russian-occupied Territories",
      "text": "Since 2014, the ruble has been used in parts of Ukraine under Russian military occupation and in Russian-occupied parts of Georgia.",
      "date": "2014"
    }
  ]
}

