      "headline": "Rise of Kashmiri Shaivism",
      "text": "Kashmiri Shaivism, a school of monistic non-theism, emerged in the Kashmir region around the 8th to 9th centuries CE, focusing on the philosophy of recognizing the divine within oneself.",
      "date": "0800"
