      "text": "The Office of Strategic Services (OSS) was established on June 13, 1942, as an intelligence agency of the United States during World War II. It was formed as an agency of the Joint Chiefs of Staff to coordinate espionage activities behind enemy lines for all branches of the United States Armed Forces.",
