      "text": "On October 17, 1989, at 5:04 p.m. local time, the Loma Prieta earthquake occurred at the Central Coast of California. The shock was centered in The Forest of Nisene Marks State Park in Santa Cruz County, approximately 10 miles northeast of Santa Cruz on a section of the San Andreas Fault System. It had an Mw magnitude of 6.9 and a maximum Modified Mercalli intensity of IX (Violent).",
