      "headline": "Construction of the Temple of Zeus",
      "text": "The Temple of Zeus, one of the most significant structures in Olympia, was constructed around 470-456 BCE. It housed the statue of Zeus, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.",
      "date": "-0470"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Statue of Zeus",
      "text": "The Statue of Zeus at Olympia, created by the sculptor Phidias, was completed around 435 BCE. This statue was considered one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.",
      "date": "-0435"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Emperor Theodosius I Bans the Games",
      "text": "In 393 AD, Roman Emperor Theodosius I banned all pagan festivals, including the Olympic Games, as part of his efforts to promote Christianity.",
      "date": "0393"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction of the Temple of Zeus",
      "text": "The Temple of Zeus was severely damaged by earthquakes in 522 and 551 AD, leading to its eventual abandonment.",
      "date": "0551"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rediscovery of Olympia",
      "text": "The site of Olympia was rediscovered in the 18th century, with systematic excavation beginning in 1829 by French archaeologists.",
      "date": "1829"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Restoration of the Olympic Games",
      "text": "In 1894, the Olympic Games were restored on a global basis, inspired by the ancient games held in Olympia. The first modern Olympics were held in Athens in 1896.",
      "date": "1894"
    }
  ]
}

